uiter Lite, Sales Navigator\nCore and Advanced customers. Premium Career plan subscribers do not have access\nto Custom Button.\n\n \n\nFooter Mercado English\n\nThis email was intended for Yashica Lohar (Flipkart GWC 7.0 Scholar CSE ’28 @\nIIIT Jabalpur 2 ⭐ @Codechef)\nLearn why we included this.\n[https://t1.em.linkedin.com/r/?id=heba62d56-5df9-416c-89a1-669285a87fc4,7c24b6,507bd8&e=bWNpZD03MjYyNTY5ODEwMzc3NDk0NTI4JnRyaz1lbWwtbWt0Zy1wcmVtLWFjcS1mdC1idXNpbmVzcy11cG0mc3JjPWUtZW1s&s=jX_AYFwUPl9S7p_Pk-RdbohGCkbbIqJ_mf5ImY4qDak]\n\nThis is an occasional email to help you get the most out of LinkedIn.\n\n Unsubscribe\n[https://t1.em.linkedin.com/r/?id=heba62d56-5df9-416c-89a1-669285a87fc4,7c24b6,507bd9&e=bWNpZD03MjYyNTY5ODEwMzc3NDk0NTI4JnRyaz1lbWwtbWt0Zy1wcmVtLWFjcS1mdC1idXNpbmVzcy11cG0mc3JjPWUtZW1sJnAxPUFRR1RDLWFzVmt1eTNnQUFBWnpnN1lsM0pHUnhFd0pCMUFUelVQWUc2ZVNzQVZRNzJMakJrSG5BU0J5YzgyUU5jc3FlY1YycC1ralJrOU53TFcwJnAyPTQ2NjkwNjMmcDM9ODEzNTg2MiZwND0yMDI2LTA0LTE1&s=m-s-C19FHE9qlTB2K6KD8dzGQeKfZfW7xqa_60_Rii8] ·  Help\n[https://t1.em.linkedin.com/r/?id=heba62d56-5df9-416c-89a1-669285a87fc4,7c24b6,507bb2&e=bWNpZD03MjYyNTY5ODEwMzc3NDk0NTI4JnRyaz1lbWwtbWt0Zy1wcmVtLWFjcS1mdC1idXNpbmVzcy11cG0mc3JjPWUtZW1s&s=BxM25VmW7Mqr4uFxXTkqRAi30o8JuV9hqNj1o0TdjNM]\nLinkedIn\n[https://res1.em.linkedin.com/res/tracking/linkedin-blue-80x20.png]https://t1.em.linkedin.com/r/?id=heba62d56-5df9-416c-89a1-669285a87fc4,7c24b6,507bb3&e=bWNpZD03MjYyNTY5ODEwMzc3NDk0NTI4JnRyaz1lbWwtbWt0Zy1wcmVtLWFjcS1mdC1idXNpbmVzcy11cG0mc3JjPWUtZW1s&s=X25IFtSTM1NR2b1h6oCZWKV2y4dsXLQbQVjIiSCEYSc\n©2026, LinkedIn Ireland Unlimited Company. All rights reserved.\nLinkedIn Ireland Unlimited Company, Gardner House, Wilton Plaza, Wilton Place,\nDublin 2, Ireland.\nLinkedIn and the LinkedIn logo are registered trademarks of LinkedIn.\n\n \n\n[https://t1.em.linkedin.com/r/?id=heba62d56-5df9-416c-89a1-669285a87fc4,7c24b6,1]','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a442209c-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear LinkedIn Premium,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"Yashica, thanks for being a valued member\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a451b4d8-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'India Industry Insights\n\nBy Accenture in India\n\n\nBy Accenture in India\n\n    \n    \n    Read this article on LinkedIn to join the conversation\nRead on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/how-humans-agentic-ai-redefining-work-skills-scale-enterprises-9fbsc?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BaYDIE7eaRiyVqrF%2F5xVHOA%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=1Zyq8uRSxtLsc1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_-null-icq8ji~mo0ymsav~ox-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mo0ymsav-ox\n  \nAs agentic systems scale across enterprises, AI is advancing at an unprecedented pace—beginning to rival human reasoning, creativity, and decision‑making. This acceleration is fundamentally reshaping how organizations think about intelligence at work. AI is no longer confined to discrete tools or isolated use cases; it is evolving into a form of co‑intelligence that works alongside people. In this model, humans remain firmly in the lead, while AI enhances judgment, accelerates execution, and increases autonomy across workflows. Accenture’s latest research with The Wharton School, ‘The Age of Co‑Intelligence,’ underscores this shift toward a skills‑first economy deeply integrated with AI. We are entering a new era in which humans and intelligent systems collaborate continuously, each amplifying the other’s strengths. AI brings speed, scale, and pattern recognition. Humans contribute context, creativity, ethics, and trust. The true value emerges where these capabilities intersect. What is changing is not just the technology, but the very nature of work itself—how decisions are made, how value is created, and how organizations stay relevant in a constantly evolving environment. Realizing this potential requires more than AI adoption. It demands rethinking operating models, talent strategies, and leadership approaches to enable continuous reinvention at enterprise scale. Read Report | Discuss News and Views From Prompts to Platforms: How Agentic AI Is Rewiring the Enterprise & Driving Reinvention Agentic AI is ushering in a reset for the enterprise, shifting from prompt‑based tools to intelligent systems that can plan, reason, and execute across workflows. It has evolved into a veritable new operating layer that sits above core enterprise systems, enabling faster decisions and smarter execution at scale. In an article in ET CIO, Dr. Milind Desai, MD – AI & Data, Accenture in India, explores how agentic AI is driving structural reinvention across functions from R&D and sales to finance and learning. Read More | Discuss India’s AI Shift: How Agentic AI Is Moving from Pilots to Enterprise‑Wide Impact Indian enterprises are accelerating AI adoption and moving beyond assistive tools to deploying agentic systems, marking a fundamental shift in how they operate, scale, and deliver value. In a Financial Express industry story, Aditya Priyadarshan, MD & Lead – AI, Accenture in India, expresses his views that agentic AI has rapidly moved from isolated pilots to enterprise-scale deployment. He highlights Accenture research that notes 86% of C-suite leaders in India view AI agents as catalysts for transformation and growth. Read More | Discuss Accenture Report: Indian Enterprises Reposition AI for Reinvention and Growth Accenture’s latest Pulse of Change 2026 research shows that business leaders are moving beyond viewing AI as a productivity or cost-efficiency lever. India findings from the survey note that nearly 90% of C-suite leaders plan to increase their AI investments in 2026. An Economic Times coverage of the findings features a quote by Saurabh Sahu, MD & Lead – India Business, Accenture, on how the biggest barrier is no longer technology, it is ensuring employees feel equipped, included and confident as AI reshapes how work gets done. In an article by Dataquest, Aditya Priyadarshan, MD & Lead – AI, Accenture in India, shares that this transition marks a fundamental shift in how Indian enterprises pursue growth and innovation across banking, life sciences, consumer goods, and retail industries. More Media Coverage: Business World | The Indian Express Accenture Report: Agentic AI and the New Rules of Platform Strategy Agentic AI is redefining platforms by reshaping how work is done, value is created, and humans and machines collaborate. This shift is most powerful when strategy keeps pace with technology. According to Accenture’s latest report on ‘The New Rules of Platform Strategy in the Age of Agentic AI,’ organizations that align their AI, platform, and business strategies see 2.2x revenue growth and a 37% EBITDA uplift. As AI becomes foundational, platform strategy is no longer optional—it is critical to winning. The report outlines five priorities to help companies succeed in an AI‑first world. Read More Acquisition of Faculty to Boost Accenture’s AI Delivery Accenture has completed the acquisition of Faculty, a leading UK‑based AI company. Faculty is recognised for its deep technical expertise and leadership in responsible AI across sectors. Faculty CEO and co‑founder Dr. Marc Warner will now serve as Accenture’s Chief Technology Officer. The acquisition strengthens Accenture’s ability to deliver safe, secure, outcome‑driven AI and Agentic AI at scale. Read More | Discuss How Our Recent Investments in Agentic AI-led Companies are Boosting Reinvention Across Key Industries ·       Consumer Goods & Retail: Accenture has invested in DaVinci Commerce, a leader in the rapidly emerging agentic AI-powered commerce, to advance Agentic AI-led shopping. Read More ·       Retail: We have also invested in Profitmind—a retail technology company that has developed an agentic AI platform to help retailers automate decisions across pricing, inventory and planning—to drive Agentic AI reinvention in the retail sector. Read More ·       Life Sciences: Accenture has invested in Ryght AI—a platform provider that modernizes how clinical research is designed and executed for the life sciences industry—to help Life Sciences companies transform clinical research with Agentic AI. Read More ·       Banking: Accenture has also invested in Lyzr, an AI company that has developed a full-stack enterprise agent infrastructure platform, to bring Agentic AI to banking and insurance companies. Read More Accenture is ready to help as you begin to reimagine your business. If you’d like to know more about how we can partner with you in your Reinvention journey, please feel free to contact us. For careers in Consulting at Accenture, please visit our Careers Portal.\nKeep reading on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/how-humans-agentic-ai-redefining-work-skills-scale-enterprises-9fbsc?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BaYDIE7eaRiyVqrF%2F5xVHOA%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=1Zyq8uRSxtLsc1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_-null-icq8ji~mo0ymsav~ox-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mo0ymsav-ox\n  \n      \n\n----------------------------------------\n\nThis email was intended for Yashica Lohar (Flipkart GWC 7.0 Scholar | CSE ’28 @ IIIT Jabalpur | 2 ⭐ @Codechef)\nLearn why we included this: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/4788?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BaYDIE7eaRiyVqrF%2F5xVH