roved-draft-placeholder','OUTGOING',NULL,'2026-06-21 17:35:51',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a5b611b3-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[https://h2svision.github.io/publicAssets/solutionChallenge2026/sc-prototype.png]\n\n \n\nDear Yashica Lohar,\n\n\nThe energy in today’s session was incredible! It’s clear that everyone is ready\nto shift gears from simply brainstorming ideas to actually taking action.\n\n\nToday wasn’t just about theory; we rolled up our sleeves and looked at how to\npractically approach your solution, think outside the box, and shape a project\nthat truly stands out. If you were there, you walked away with more than just a\nroadmap-you walked away with momentum.\n\nGet hands-on with Gemma! Access the project file shared by our speaker right\nhere:\n\n\n\nClick here for the source file\n[https://9hdppg0c.r.ap-southeast-2.awstrack.me/L0/https:%2F%2Fhuggingface.co%2Fspaces%2Frishiraj%2Fgemma4-insurance/1/0108019db575d2fa-9996d101-c443-4734-a5d3-fd87285110f7-000000/kLQjNKRj1cAn1ukohV3ckaVdaac=256] \n\n\nNext steps in-line\n\nAs we’re in the final phase of the hackathon and prototype submissions deadline\nis officially closing soon. \n\n\nIt’s time for you to start submitting your prototypes, and don’t wait for the\nlast-minute rush. \n\n\nTake help from the 6-step treasure guide, that has been specially curated by us\nto help you for the prototype submissions. \n\n \n\nClick Here for the Treasure Guide\n[https://9hdppg0c.r.ap-southeast-2.awstrack.me/L0/https:%2F%2Fdocs.google.com%2Fdocument%2Fd%2F1nBtrGqdJWuIOOMAVkw3rfKohoaTMl8UyOYf4QB3qADs%2Fedit%3Fusp=sharing/1/0108019db575d2fa-9996d101-c443-4734-a5d3-fd87285110f7-000000/WB1SB7cc2MvEuiHxoZRBkQpER1E=256]\n\n\nSubmit your prototype now with all core features intact. Think of this as your\n\"anchor\" submission—it ensures you have a seat at the table even if things get\nhectic.\nYou can continue to refine, polish, and update your submission as the deadline\napproaches.\n\n\nRegards,\n\nTeam Hack2skill\n\n \n\n \n\nFacebook\n[https://h2svision.github.io/publicAssets/vision/h2s_facebook.png]https://9hdppg0c.r.ap-southeast-2.awstrack.me/L0/https:%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Fhack2skill%2F/1/0108019db575d2fa-9996d101-c443-4734-a5d3-fd87285110f7-000000/Zfav79-UJQuTyvjxvXG2JmnHEbU=256\nTwitter\n[https://h2svision.github.io/publicAssets/vision/h2s_twitter.png]https://9hdppg0c.r.ap-southeast-2.awstrack.me/L0/https:%2F%2Ftwitter.com%2Fhack2skill/1/0108019db575d2fa-9996d101-c443-4734-a5d3-fd87285110f7-000000/xFOwg5MquyHc4hXbWtWea5jUpY8=256\nInstagram\n[https://h2svision.github.io/publicAssets/vision/h2s_instagram.png]https://9hdppg0c.r.ap-southeast-2.awstrack.me/L0/https:%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Fhack2skill%2F/1/0108019db575d2fa-9996d101-c443-4734-a5d3-fd87285110f7-000000/4VaLftVGw_687AgCF3DbzSPcYNY=256\nLinkedIn\n[https://h2svision.github.io/publicAssets/vision/h2s_linkedin.png]https://9hdppg0c.r.ap-southeast-2.awstrack.me/L0/https:%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Fcompany%2Fhack2skill%2F/1/0108019db575d2fa-9996d101-c443-4734-a5d3-fd87285110f7-000000/qm61dxo72s1miaW9ed5JkhWljh8=256\nYouTube\n[https://h2svision.github.io/publicAssets/vision/h2s_youtube.png]https://9hdppg0c.r.ap-southeast-2.awstrack.me/L0/https:%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fchannel%2FUCw2br80x_dpvJoAsSCC-bGA/1/0108019db575d2fa-9996d101-c443-4734-a5d3-fd87285110f7-000000/p0QqlK0u0uNGr6Ev08HPc6vA-IM=256\nWhatsApp\n[https://h2svision.github.io/publicAssets/vision/h2s_whatsapp.png]https://9hdppg0c.r.ap-southeast-2.awstrack.me/L0/https:%2F%2Fapi.whatsapp.com%2Fsend%2F%3Fphone=919870330830%26text%26type=phone_number%26app_absent=0/1/0108019db575d2fa-9996d101-c443-4734-a5d3-fd87285110f7-000000/tXjNa3v7RME09K8zRpDcGhvWo7w=256\nDiscord\n[https://h2svision.github.io/publicAssets/vision/h2s_discord.png]https://9hdppg0c.r.ap-southeast-2.awstrack.me/L0/https:%2F%2Fdiscord.com%2Fchannels%2F900275142217830402%2F969491518371008562/1/0108019db575d2fa-9996d101-c443-4734-a5d3-fd87285110f7-000000/O_gDm48NItdw0vWwxi-4ondeb38=256\n\n© 2026. Built on Hack2skill\n[https://9hdppg0c.r.ap-southeast-2.awstrack.me/L0/https:%2F%2Fhack2skill.com%2F/1/0108019db575d2fa-9996d101-c443-4734-a5d3-fd87285110f7-000000/GCrNDIiqC3vgdV-y5VEYn0yHEyo=256]\n\n[https://9hdppg0c.r.ap-southeast-2.awstrack.me/I0/0108019db575d2fa-9996d101-c443-4734-a5d3-fd87285110f7-000000/r0Y-eEgNBlajzFExM3DSd_4R-TE=256]','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a5b6964a-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear Solution Challenge 2026 - Build with AI,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"Momentum check: Time to start submitting your prototypes\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a5bf53bc-6d97-11f1-89d5-e86538d58b3c','e754e5ff-6703-11f1-a09a-8107a00d61c0','How to Position Your Podcast to be Sold for a Profit','newsletters-noreply@linkedin.com','loharyashica@gmail.com',NULL,'Podcasting Made Simple\n\nBy Alex Sanfilippo\n\n\nBy Alex Sanfilippo\n\n    \n    \n    Read this article on LinkedIn to join the conversation\nRead on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/how-position-your-podcast-sold-profit-alex-sanfilippo-xoeie?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BacmT1fUHRcerO9wlAxZXWQ%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=0u3t5ttsja5Ik1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_-null-icq8ji~mqgpos27~lm-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mqgpos27-lm\n  \nMost podcasters never consider selling their show, even when it’s the right next step. But, perhaps, it’s time for you to start exploring selling your podcast! In this episode, Anjel B Hartwell explains exactly how a podcast is real intellectual property you can package, transfer, and make a win-win for you and the buyer. Get ready to understand the process, protect your value, and make a smart exit when the time is right! 🎧 Watch or Listen to This Episode of Podcasting Made Simple: https://PodMatch.com/Episodes (Then Search \"388\") 📝 Big Ideas From This Episode: 1. Treat your podcast like IP A podcast is an asset, not just content. Build it like intellectual property with clear positioning, repeatable systems, and transferable value. 2. Sell the brand, not the episodes Buyers pay for what the brand unlocks: a name that fits their mission, trust with listeners, and a shortcut to credibility they did not have to build. 3. Package the assets buyers want Line up what transfers cleanly: feed access, artwork, website, email list, guest Rolodex, social handles, and any templates or playbooks that run the show. 4. Document your SOPs Simple operating procedures raise value because the buyer can keep quality steady. Even step by step production checklists can justify a higher price. 5. Prove traction with real signals Have proof ready: rankings, back catalog depth, countries reached, download trends, email engagement, and audience fit. Buyers want evidence, not vibes. Attend Podcasting Made Simple Live For Free by visiting https://PodMatch.com/event and use code PMLIVE! 6. Use the SHELL selling frame Stand your ground, hold space, educate and evaluate, love what you sell, then let go. It keeps the conversation calm, confident, and pressure free. 7. Evaluate the buyer as much as they do Check character, capability, and alignment with your listeners. If the buyer cannot serve the audience well, the deal will feel wrong even if the money is right. 8. Price the shortcut you created You are selling years of momentum. A buyer is paying to shorten their learning curve and skip the slow ramp of building trust, process, and positioning. 9. Expect bumps, design for clarity Even good deals hit friction. Write terms clearly, define what is included, and keep communication tight so the transfer does not drift or stall. 10. Keep relationships at the center The best exits come from trust. When you protect the listener and treat the buyer like a partner, you leave with a clean reputation and future opportunities. 💡 Final Thought: A profitable podcast sale is rarely magic. It is the result of trust, consistency, and a brand people want to inherit. When hosts and guests build real relationships, the show becomes more than content. It becomes a network, a reputation, and a set of opportunities that can outlive the original creator. 💬 Did you listen to or watch this episode of Podcasting Made Simple? If yes, what was your biggest takeaway?\nKeep reading on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/how-position-your-podcast-sold-profit-alex-sanfilippo-xoeie?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BacmT1fUHRcerO9wlAxZXWQ%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=0u3t5ttsja5Ik1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_-null-icq8ji~mqgpos27~lm-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mqgpos27-lm\n  \n      \n\n----------------------------------------\n\nThis email was intended for Yashica Lohar (Flipkart GWC 7.0 Scholar | CSE ’28 @ IIIT Jabalpur | 2 ⭐ @Codechef)\nLearn why we included this: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/4788?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BacmT1fUHRcerO9wlAxZXWQ%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=0u3t5ttsja5Ik1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mqgpos27~lm-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mqgpos27-lm\nYou are receiving LinkedIn notification emails. Others can see that you are a subscriber.\n\n\nUnsubscribe: https://www.linkedin.com/series-notifications/?action=unsubscribe&memberToken=ADoAAEIlwb4B7wSObgzu320