ur team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a653f5ce-6d97-11f1-89d5-e86538d58b3c','e754e5ff-6703-11f1-a09a-8107a00d61c0','Re: Trying WebSockets and Webhooks','brian.lee+api@coingecko.com','loharyashica@gmail.com',NULL,'Would these help what you\'re building?‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ \n\n\nHi ,\n\n\nBrian here from the CoinGecko API team. Thanks for building with the CoinGecko API.\n\n\nIn case you missed it, we recently launched two new ways to get data from CoinGecko. Altogether, we now offerthree native data delivery methods:\n * REST [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=7LW&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hy85rrr&](Pull):For on-demand and bulk data requests.\n   \n * WebSocket [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=7L6&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hr3grJF&](Stream):Persistent connection to stream sub-second and tick-by-tick market data.\n   \n * Webhook [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=7LV&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hpOeFyM&](Push):Receive automated push notifications exactly when a data change event occurs.\n   \n\nBoth WebSocket and Webhooks aren\'t part of the free Demo plan as of now.\n\n\n[https://multimedia.newsletter.coingecko.com/coingecko-h/photos/15fa79bd-8f9d-4821-a475-98ce01245753.png]\n\nI\'d like to understand what you\'re working on and whether either of these new data delivery methods would be useful for you. If we think they\'re a fit for what you\'re building, I\'d also be glad to grant access for you to try them.\n\n\nLet me know your thoughts by filling up the quick form below and I\'ll take it from there:\n\n\n👉Feedback Survey Link [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=7LY&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=h2fI3wo&]\n\n\nCheers,\nBrian Lee\nGrowth @ CoinGecko API\nwww.coingecko.com/api [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=7LL&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hprzcoW&]\n\n\n\nCoinGecko API for Business [https://multimedia.newsletter.coingecko.com/coingecko-h/photos/c3c6798f-315a-4d03-9fa6-7f5b8191d2cc.png]\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nYou may unsubscribe [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/unsubscribe.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&m=dYX&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=h2l90HM&] or change your contact details [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/change_details.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&m=dYX&s=T0i3&u=p&z=h4IwcoG&] at any time.\n','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 17:35:52',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a654a17f-6d97-11f1-89d5-e86538d58b3c','e754e5ff-6703-11f1-a09a-8107a00d61c0','Re: Re: Trying WebSockets and Webhooks','loharyashica@gmail.com','brian.lee+api@coingecko.com',NULL,'Dear Brian from CoinGecko,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"Re: Trying WebSockets and Webhooks\".\n\nYour reference ID is #e754e5ff. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','OUTGOING',NULL,'2026-06-21 17:35:52',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a65b21d8-6d97-11f1-89d5-e86538d58b3c','e754e5ff-6703-11f1-a09a-8107a00d61c0','Like music? Want to learn the future of retail? Join me in 20 min','newsletters-noreply@linkedin.com','loharyashica@gmail.com',NULL,'LinkedIn 360 l By GaryVee\n\nBy Gary Vaynerchuk\n\n\nBy Gary Vaynerchuk\n\n    \n    \n    Read this article on LinkedIn to join the conversation\nRead on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/like-music-want-learn-future-retail-join-me-20-min-gary-vaynerchuk-sdcze?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BKMLaM3DQQOqSs0mOyH15TQ%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=2Urc9uBPkt8Yk1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_-null-icq8ji~mqjubkh6~od-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mqjubkh6-od\n  \nA new soundtrack is dropping this summer. As you may know, VeeFriends is my digital and physical collectibles brand. I\'m building the next Pokémon, and we have an exciting new announcement. VeeFriends and Bose just teamed up for something we\'ve been so excited to share: a limited-edition VeeFriends × Bose SoundLink Flex Bluetooth Speaker (Gen 2), dropping in collectible blind boxes with three characters that are perfect for the summer. BBQ, beach trip, and rooftop hangs just got that much more memorable. Every pull is a surprise! Pull Flex\'n Fox and Swaggy Sea Lion (both at 1:2 odds of pulling), or hunt for the Rare Robot (1:19 odds of pulling). This drop goes LIVE Thursday, June 18 from 3pm ET to 5pm ET in a BOSE Mega Live Drop Show hosted by GaryVee. Set your reminder. This is going to be a fun one! Fast Facts: Product: VeeFriends × Bose SoundLink Flex Bluetooth Speaker (Gen 2) Format: Randomized blind box, one (1) speaker per box Variants & odds: Flex\'n Fox - 1:2 odds of pulling, Swaggy Sea Lion - 1:2 odds of pulling, Rare Robot - 1:19 odds of pulling Price: $159.00 per blind box Shipping: All orders ship by Monday, June 22 Live drop: BOSE Mega Live Drop Show hosted by GaryVee Live drop date: Thursday, June 18 Live drop time: 3pm ET to 5pm ET Live drop show: https://garyvee.com/bose Holder claims: 1 randomized blind box speaker per NFT Eligible Holders: Series 1 Spectacular Flex\'n Fox, Swaggy Sealion, Rare Robot Holder claim window: Thursday, June 18th @ 12 PM ET - Thursday, July 2nd @ 12 PM ET Holder claim access: https://shop.veefriends.com/collections/holder-claims A Closer Look At The VeeFriends × Bose SoundLink Flex Speaker The VeeFriends × Bose SoundLink Flex Speaker is customized with three original VeeFriends character designs. Every speaker contains the same big sound, rugged build, and up to 12 hours of battery life. Each blind box contains one (1) speaker, and there are a limited number of speakers available. Flex\'n Fox Flex\'n Fox knows how to throw a party, as he\'s confident with the flex, charismatic, and always ready to crank up the volume. The \"Turn It Up!\" art treatment captures that energy across the speaker\'s red-grilled face. There are 1:2 odds of pulling this box. Swaggy Sea Lion Swaggy Sea Lion brings the boombox-on-the-shoulder, summer-on-the-boardwalk vibe. Wrapped around a purple grill, the sea lion + boombox art is built for poolside, beachside, and every open window in between. There are 1:2 odds of pulling this box. Rare Robot Rare Robot is the ultimate chase in this drop, with a \"Theme Song\" art treatment on a blue grill that signals it\'s time to blast some tunes to match your main character energy. There are 1:19 odds of pulling this box. How To Get Your VeeFriends × Bose SoundLink Flex Speaker The entire drop goes live exclusively on Whatnot during the BOSE Mega Live Drop Show, hosted by GaryVee. What: VeeFriends × Bose SoundLink Flex Bluetooth Speaker (blind box, 1 speaker per box) Who: Open to anyone Price: $159.00 per blind box When: Thursday, June 18 @ 3pm ET to 5pm ET Where: veefriends.com/live With a limited amount of speakers available, tune in early as this drop is going to move. PLEASE NOTE: All orders ship by Monday, June 22 Holder Claims Who: Series 1 Spectacular Flex\'n Fox, Swaggy Sea Lion, & Rare Robot What: VeeFriends × Bose SoundLink Flex Bluetooth Speaker Claim limits: 1 Randomized Blind Box Speaker per NFT When: Thursday, June 18 @ 12 PM ET - Thursday, July 2 @ 12 PM ET Where: https://shop.veefriends.com/collections/holder-claims This is the collab that just made your summer plans better. Grab yours before they\'re gone! Blind boxes don\'t last, and neither does summer.\nKeep reading on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/like-music-want-learn-future-retail-join-me-20-min-gary-vaynerchuk-sdcze?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BKMLaM3DQQOqSs0mOyH15TQ%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BF