 Reinventing How Work Works: Fusion Agentic Applications, on April 30 to learn more. What are Agentic Applications? Oracle Fusion Agentic Applications are designed to help organizations unlock time, capacity, and outcomes that were previously out of reach. Instead of waiting for instructions and assisting users, these applications carry work forward by reasoning, deciding, and acting in pursuit of defined business goals. They are: Outcome-driven: They go beyond task-based automation to focus on defined business objectives – such as closing the books faster, lowering supplier costs, or increasing expansion revenue – and take the actions required to achieve them. Proactive and reasoning-based: They continuously monitor activity, filter signal from noise, identify what requires action, and take the appropriate next steps at the right time. Built for enterprise execution: They operate within existing Oracle Fusion Applications governance, security, approval, and audit frameworks, with clear visibility into what the system did and why. This enables Fusion Agentic Applications to know when to act autonomously and when to involve a person so actions can be executed safely. Powered by agent teams: They use coordinated groups of specialized AI agents that collaborate, analyze, recommend, and execute actions across processes to achieve a defined outcome.  In short, they don’t just assist, they act. The Built-In Advantage Fusion Agentic Applications work because the AI agents are built into the system that already runs the business. In other words, they’re not operating outside of the system or stitching together disconnected tools in the same way that copilots, AI assistants, or other AI add-ons do. They eliminate the need for humans to connect processes across systems. Embedded within Oracle Fusion Cloud Applications, the AI agents can securely use the same enterprise data, workflows, policies, approval hierarchies, permissions, and history that teams rely on every day. This enables them to act in real time, at enterprise scale, with governance built in. What Does This Look Like in Action? When put into practice, Fusion Agentic Applications both surface insights and complete the work necessary to achieve set business objectives, such as:  Fewer payroll issues and faster workforce scheduling: The Workforce Operations Agentic Application helps HR leaders reduce manual data gathering, accelerate scheduling request approvals, and reduce payroll issues. Lower supplier sourcing costs: The Design-to-Source Workspace Agentic Application helps supply chain leaders reduce product cost, cycle time, and compliance risk. Higher win rates, lower customer acquisition costs: The Cross-Sell Program Workspace Agentic Application helps sales teams identify growth opportunities, drive predictable expansion revenue, and lower customer acquisition costs. Faster cash collection: The Collectors Workspace Agentic Application helps finance teams collect cash faster, lower days sales outstanding, and achieve higher promise to pay conversion. In each agentic application, the agents take ownership of the workflow (gathering information, coordinating next steps, making decisions, and executing actions) so that work progresses without constant human intervention, and we can spend more time on judgment, creativity, and the strategic decisions that matter. Expanding the Fusion AI Ecosystem Fusion Agentic Applications are supported by Oracle’s growing AI ecosystem anchored by Oracle AI Agent Studio. With the Agentic Applications Builder in AI Agent Studio, organizations can build, connect, and run agentic applications using Oracle, partner, and external agents without traditional application development. This is only the beginning of the rise of a more autonomous enterprise.   Join my LinkedIn Live, Reinventing How Work Works: Fusion Agentic Applications on April 30 to learn more. - Chris Leone, EVP of Applications Development, Oracle\nKeep reading on LinkedIn\nhttps:/