think it is. Companies and employees looking to take full advantage of AI aren’t asking what it can do. They\'re examining what AI can help them become — like a brand with a personality, a marketer who never misses, or a manager of both humans and agents. That\'s a fundamentally different game. In this issue, we cover why naming your agent is a bigger decision than you think, how AI makes audience targeting a huge advantage for small businesses, and what it looks like when contact center supervisors stop playing defense. FinalAgentFinal_v2_FinalFinal What takes more time, building an agent or naming one? While building is only getting easier, choosing the right name can send you down a rabbit hole. Going with a human name can break down the psychological barriers of interacting with a machine, while a functional title like “timesheet agent” can set clear expectations. Here’s what to consider when naming an agent. Once you’ve decided, make sure you check what the name means in other languages. Otherwise, you might make a “siri” of yourself. Stop playing with your food (and marketing budget) Throwing spaghetti at the wall. Kitchen sink marketing. Fishing with dynamite. Whatever you call your strategy, if you’re not using AI to zero in on your audience, you’re wasting time and money.  That’s especially true for small businesses with tight budgets. With its ability to analyze site clicks, service logs, and purchase history, AI lets every company predict what a customer will do next. Turn your data into customer segments and start delivering perfectly timed, personalized offers that rival the biggest brands in the world. Service team maestro As the number of ways to contact customer service has increased, so has the need for oversight and coordination. Who can contact center leaders call (or chat or text or email or WhatsApp) when they need help? Themselves. Thanks to AI-powered service tools.  With a full view of their customer service data, managers can spot trends before they become full-blown crises, jump in to coach human reps, or refine AI training data in real time. It’s a shift that turns exhausted managers into proactive, indispensable leaders with bandwidth to build high-performing teams. While you were prompting … stories you may have missed from the world of AI The next time a CAPTCHA asks you for proof of life, you may want to confirm it’s not a human. That’s because millions of people are pretending to be AI chatbots online. Just enter a prompt in the chatbox at youraislopbores.me and you’ll receive a human-written response. You can also take your turn acting like a chatbot, with a 60-second countdown to answer a random human’s question. That’s plenty of time to ask ChatGPT to ghostwrite your response. This newsletter was curated by Benny Spiewak, Senior Marketing Lead at Salesforce.\nKeep reading on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/bob-bot-how-name-your-agent-salesforce-do6qc?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3B7P1ptaMHQuCHFdUwUtw%2FrQ%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=1MhVfDjLXy0Yg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_-null-icq8ji~moivmdwk~7h-null-null&eid=icq8ji-moivmdwk-7h\n  \n      \n\n----------------------------------------\n\nThis email was intended for Yashica Lohar (Flipkart GWC 7.0 Scholar | CSE ’28 @ IIIT Jabalpur | 2 ⭐ @Codechef)\nLearn why we included this: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/4788?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3B7P1ptaMHQuCHFdUwUtw%2FrQ%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=1MhVfDjLXy0Yg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~moivmdwk~7h-null-null&eid=icq8ji-moivmdwk-7h\nYou are receiving LinkedIn notification emails. Others can see that you are a subscriber.\n\n\nUnsubscribe: https://www.linkedin.com/series-notifications/?action=unsubscribe&memberToken=ADoAAEIlwb4B7wSObgzu320aKxhPrfHhU2UtxwY&newsletterId=7079504890934263808&newsletterTitle=Do More With AI&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3B7P1ptaMHQuCHFdUwUtw%2FrQ%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=1MhVfDjLXy0Yg1&ek=email_series_follow_newsletter_02&e=icq8ji-moivmdwk-7h&eid=icq8ji-moivmdwk-7h&m=unsubscribe&ts=footerGlimmer&li=0&t=plh    ·  Help: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/67?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3B7P1ptaMHQuCHFdUwUtw%2FrQ%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=1MhVfDjLXy0Yg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-help-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-help-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~moivmdwk~7h-null-null&eid=icq8ji-moivmdwk-7h\n\n© 2026 LinkedIn Corporation, 1zwnj000 West Maude Avenue, Sunnyvale, CA 94085.\nLinkedIn and the LinkedIn logo are registered trademarks of LinkedIn.','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a6d4be1c-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear Do More With AI,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"Bob or Bot? How To Name Your Agent\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a6e160a5-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hello yashi_11,\n\nYou are welcome to register and compete in Codeforces Round 1096 (Div. 3). It starts on Thursday, April, 30, 2026 14:35 (UTC). The contest duration is 2.5 hours. The allowed programming languages are C/C++, Python, Java, Kotlin, Rust, Go, C#, F#, Pascal/Delphi, JavaScript, D, Haskell, OCaml, Perl, PHP, Ruby, Scala.\n\nDiv. 3 rounds are designed especially for participants with a rating below 1600. You are invited to participate in the competition!\n\nThe goal of such rounds is to help beginner participants to gain skills and to get new knowledge in a real contest. You can read the details in this post. In short:\n\n* Not only real problems, but also exercises can be used.\n* Our main goal is to give you effective training problems, the novelty of the problems isn\'t the priority.\n* Text of the statements is often formal.\n* Rated for participant with the rating below 1600.\n* ICPC rules + 12-hour open hacking phase.\n* Untrusted participants are not included in the official ranklist.\n\nThe round will be held on the rules of Educational Rounds, so read the rules (here) beforehand. The round will be for newbies and participants with a rating below 1600. Want to compete? Do not forget to register for the contest and check your handle on the registrants page. The registration will be open for the whole duration of the contest.\n\nIf you have any questions, please feel free to ask me on the pages of Codeforces. If you no longer wish to receive these emails, click https://codeforces.com/unsubscribe/contests/b5b5e0b2a2aa71a8ed4b7966676c3e6212f3c08a/ to unsubscribe.\n\nWish you high rating, Mike Mirzayanov and Codeforces team\n\n','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a6e1f540-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear Valued Customer,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"Codeforces Round 1096 (Div. 3)\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a6f64033-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'NamasteDev Logo [https://do6gp1uxl3luu.cloudfront.net/banner+and+logos/name.png]\n\nNamaste!\n\nIf you\'re aiming for a software job, there’s one skill almost every company\ntests first - Data Structures and Algorithms (DSA).\n\nWhether it’s placements, internships, or job switches, strong DSA skills are\noften the difference between getting shortlisted and getting rejected.\n\n\nBUT MANY LEARNERS STRUGGLE BECAUSE THEY DON’T KNOW:\n\n• What to study\n• How to practice\n• How to prepare for interviews\n\nThat’s exactly why we built Namaste DSA - a structured, beginner-friendly course\ndesigned to help you master problem solving and prepare confidently for coding\ninterviews.\n\n\nIN THIS COURSE, YOU\'LL 👇\n\n✅ Learn DSA from basics to advanced\n✅ Understand patterns used in real interviews\n✅ Improve problem-solving speed and confidence\n✅ Prepare effectively for placements and job switches\n\n\nWHO IS THIS COURSE FOR? 👇\n\n• Students preparing for placements.\n• Working professionals switching jobs\n• Developers struggling with DSA confidence\n• Anyone tired of random YouTube tutorials 😅\n\nGet lifetime access to interview-focused content, curated notes, AI resume\nreviewer, Practice platform and many other features for absolutely FREE !!!\n\n\n\n🎁 We have a special coupon just for you!\n\nCODE26\n\nGet your favorite course at the lowest price possible!\n\n🚀 Enroll Today\n[https://gq33w18w.r.ap-south-1.awstrack.me/L0/https:%2F%2Fnamastedev.com%2Flink%2FU00vbZs8/1/02090000o4sclilv-dknmrtag-ogc3-3q2a-u2ro-08d3h345okg0-000000/YFYB3S7lB3fPQzEj4ui10orbN7Y=256]\n\n💡 Pro Tip: Get additional discounts when you purchase course bundles!\n\nNeed help? We\'re here for you!\n\nsupport@namastedev.com [support@namastedev.com]\n\nStay Connected with Us!\n\nInstagram\n[https://gq33w18w.r.ap-south-1.awstrack.me/L0/https:%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Fnamastedevofficial/1/02090000o4sclilv-dknmrtag-ogc3-3q2a-u2ro-08d3h345okg0-000000/R5ZO4vdRl3Vnx7IoLfymo7C5rzY=256]\n| X\n[https://gq33w18w.r.ap-south-1.awstrack.me/L0/https:%2F%2Fx.com%2Fakshaymarch7/1/02090000o4sclilv-dknmrtag-ogc3-3q2a-u2ro-08d3h345okg0-000000/