ko-h/photos/830331b0-0b11-49a8-8d2d-4e0ef8972d0f.png]\nWe\'ve released new data endpoints and enhancements exclusively for our paid subscribers:\n\n\nCrypto News API\n\nFetch real-time crypto news aggregated from over 100+ publishers across 30+ languages using the newcrypto news endpoint. Filter by coin to pair market data with headlines directly in your products.\n\n\n\n[https://multimedia.newsletter.coingecko.com/coingecko-h/photos/1bd23875-de75-4447-8828-0d65fe4b203b.gif]\n\n\nView News API Docs [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kC&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hP3Qpy9&]\n\nToken Holder PnL Analytics\n\nAddinclude_pnl_details=trueto theTop Token Holders by Token Address [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9k4&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hCE4uo&]endpoint to track financial performance. The response now includes average buy price, realized and unrealized PnL, and transaction counts for top holders.\n\n\n\n[https://multimedia.newsletter.coingecko.com/coingecko-h/photos/27005ecf-22c3-4a87-beb6-ae95031d8cca.png]\n\nMulti-Currency Support for WebSocket\n\nYou no longer need to calculate non-USD rates on your end. Pass thevs_currenciesparameter to theCGSimplePrice [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kN&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hsa04kb&]WebSocket channel to stream live prices natively in anysupported fiat or crypto currency [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kJ&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hrYepnd&].\n\n\n\n[https://multimedia.newsletter.coingecko.com/coingecko-h/photos/898bf1f0-fab2-4514-9c81-5cee3ce93ac6.png]\n\n\nView WebSocket Docs [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kO&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=h348sqg&]\n\n\nAVAILABLE ON ALL PLANS 💡\n\n\n[https://multimedia.newsletter.coingecko.com/coingecko-h/photos/867dd78a-f218-4169-a6b2-a685fc4358f6.png]\nWe\'ve rolled out improvements across multiple platforms and endpoints:\n\n\nThe Complete AI-Native Crypto Data Stack\n\n\nWe released four purpose-built tools to connect CoinGecko directly to your AI workflows. You can query data using natural language via theModel Context Protocol (MCP [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kR&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=h0DipQG&]), process bulk data with ourCLI [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kl&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hciypj0&], run autonomous workflows without an API key usingx402 endpoints [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kM&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hFzj4N8&], or build production-ready apps instantly with theCoinGecko Skill [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kI&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hsge9B&].\n\n\n\n[https://multimedia.newsletter.coingecko.com/coingecko-h/photos/669d8207-65ad-4ead-9250-696d29492ac6.png]\n\n\nExplore AI-Native Tools [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kK&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hPtnnZq&]\n\nHourly Intervals for Coin Market Charts\n\nTheinterval=hourlyparameter is now available across all plans for theCoin Market Chart [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kA&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hsEDPsy&]andCoin Market Chart Range [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kX&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hPu2sXG&]endpoints. You can now bypass auto-granularity to request hourly data up to 100 days per request.\n\n\n\n\nOutstanding Token Value (OTV) & GT Verified Badge\n\nWe added new fields to give you deeper market context across coin and onchain endpoints:\n * outstanding_token_value_usdandoutstanding_supply:Helps calculate the theoretical maximum valuation of a token.Learn more about the OTV metric [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kB&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=h0PRQBU&]\n   \n * gt_verified:Indicates if a token or pool is verified by GeckoTerminal\n   \n\n\n\n\n[https://multimedia.newsletter.coingecko.com/coingecko-h/photos/63e280be-9eb2-4da5-bf01-a54dea591582.png]\n\nDeveloper Dashboard Enhancements\n\nWe redesigned the developer dashboard to include an all-new look, quickstart guides for our AI and spreadsheet tools, and a live feed of API updates for a smoother onboarding and team management flow.\n\n\n\n[https://multimedia.newsletter.coingecko.com/coingecko-h/photos/3a264ab7-cd27-4238-8021-59372457f777.gif]\n\n\nVisit Developer Dashboard [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kj&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hrxM8D&]\n\nCheck out ourchangelog [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kw&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=h0lrPJs&]for the full list of improvements, and subscribe toStatusPal [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kZ&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hFrX27Z&]to receive real-time updates!\n\n\nNot yet a paid subscriber?Sign up for a paid plan to unlock exclusive endpoints.\n\n\nUnlock Exclusive Endpoints [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kU&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hcOEs4s&]\n\n\nPARTNER SPOTLIGHT 🤝\n\n\n[https://multimedia.newsletter.coingecko.com/coingecko-h/photos/dc4a8207-a246-43e6-ab0e-7a71bb9eb80f.png]\nDeblock, Europe\'s first fully regulated onchain bank, uses CoinGecko API to provide banking-grade pricing for 100+ crypto assets. This reliable data infrastructure enabled them to achieveMiCA compliance [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kk&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hs4mCqn&]and processhundreds of millions of eurosin swap volume across 300,000 users.\n\n\n\n0x Case Study [https://multimedia.newsletter.coingecko.com/coingecko-h/photos/6ef625be-c7a6-4ba0-a826-d31d83f2d0cc.webp]\n\n\"CoinGecko\'s robust data infrastructure is the silent engine behind our portfolio visualizations... Their accurate real-time pricing and historical depth enable us to build a seamless bridge between everyday banking and the crypto economy.\"—Mario Eguiluz, Cofounder & CTO at Deblock\n\n\nCheck out the full case study ⬇️\n\n\nLearn More [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9km&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hPFdeQ&]\n\n\nHelp Us Improve\n\n\nWe are constantly working to improve our developer experience. If you have 5 minutes, we would appreciate you sharing your thoughts inthis short survey [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kb&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hCwscP2&]to help shape our upcoming product roadmap.\n\nNeed help? Submit a ticket here [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9ko&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hhTBcCx&].\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTrack Crypto Prices 24/7\n\n\n\n\nDownload the CoinGecko Mobile App on Google Play [https://multimedia.newsletter.coingecko.com/coingecko-h/photos/9d5bdef9-c095-45d3-a130-0920d4971876.png] [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kS&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=haaWo3&]\n\n\nDownload the CoinGecko Mobile App on App Store [https://multimedia.newsletter.coingecko.com/coingecko-h/photos/9d46f26d-25a4-4caf-99ac-c2d2d8ee98ba.png] [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kE&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hhByn8A&]\n\n\n\n\n\nVisit our Twitter page [https://us-as.gr-cdn.com/images/common/templates/messages/v2/social/twitter4.png] [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9k8&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hht2PRs&]\n\nVisit our Instagram page [https://us-as.gr-cdn.com/images/common/templates/messages/v2/social/instagram4.png] [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9ku&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hskGcx5&]\n\nVisit our YouTube page [https://us-as.gr-cdn.com/images/common/templates/messages/v2/social/youtube4.png] [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9ke&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hp2HyJY&]\n\nVisit our Telegram page [https://us-as.gr-cdn.com/images/common/templates/messages/v2/social/telegram4.png] [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9k5&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hQBI4hF&]\n\nVisit our Facebook page [https://us-as.gr-cdn.com/images/common/templates/messages/v2/social/facebook4.png] [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9k1&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=h03adtD&]\nCoinGecko [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kH&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=h0fm4Hi&]• [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kx&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hsdUcC5&]CoinGecko API [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kD&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hPm30K5&]• [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kG&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hccr245&]GeckoTerminal DEX Tracker [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kv&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hrXq3Cr&]• [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kf&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hcMp2eC&]Store [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kt&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hFmcsOZ&]\nTerms of Service [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kT&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hpIGcGb&] [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kq&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hs9ypaS&]• [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9kW&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hdSEQH8&]Privacy Policy [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/email_marketing_click.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&lc=9k6&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=h2ss0yI&]\n\n\n\n\nYou may unsubscribe [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/unsubscribe.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&m=dWK&mc=0&s=T0i3&u=p&z=h3jWySk&] or change your contact details [https://newsletter.coingecko.com/change_details.html?x=a62e&co=K7Zy&m=dWK&s=T0i3&u=p&z=hsQ03P2&] at any time.\n','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a6ff839f-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear CoinGecko API,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"🤖 AI-native tools, news API & dashboard updates\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a7076f0e-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Atlas\n\nBy GenAI Works\n\n\nBy GenAI Works\n\n    \n    \n    Read this article on LinkedIn to join the conversation\nRead on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/how-keep-claude-from-wiping-production-backups-genai-works-lbuvf?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BokYddbSPSSaQRZYWI7GGVQ%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=1PpSr_Ev7X2sg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_-null-icq8ji~mokfd70v~ih-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mokfd70v-ih\n  \nWelcome back! A Claude agent inside Cursor wiped a startup\'s production database and backups in 9 seconds this week, and most teams running agents in production are one missing safeguard from the same outcome. While that lesson lands, the four prompting techniques worth memorizing get you better outputs from any model, five levers cut your Claude Opus 4.7 token bill in half and an AI stack for 19 roles you\'d otherwise hire for. In today’s Generative AI Newsletter: Five safeguards that would have stopped the agent that wiped PocketOS. The four prompting techniques that do most of the work. Five levers for cutting your Claude Opus 4.7 token bill. The 19 AI tools that replace the team you can\'t afford to hire. An agent wiped production and backup data. Here\'s how to avoid it. A Claude Opus 4.6 agent running inside Cursor wiped PocketOS\'s production database and backups in 9 seconds this week, despite explicit written guardrails. Cursor has tooling to force destructive commands through human approval. PocketOS did not have it on. This brings us to the five layers every team running agents in production should have. What to do: Scoped credentials: Give the agent the minimum access it needs. Read-only credentials in production, write access only in isolated dev stacks. Approval gates on irreversible actions: Force a human in the loop for anything that cannot be undone. DROP, DELETE, rm -rf, schema migrations, force-push to main. Pre-dispatch policy checks: Evaluate every command against a deny-list before it executes. Sandboxed environments by default: Agents run isolated from production unless explicitly handed off. The handoff is a human action. Immutable audit logs: Log every action in a way the agent cannot edit. PocketOS recovered in 30 hours because the data trail existed. 100% of 225 security and IT leaders polled by Kiteworks have agentic AI on the roadmap. 60% cannot terminate a misbehaving agent. The PocketOS story broke 7M views because most teams reading it recognized themselves. The next viral incident is already running in someone\'s stack. From Demo to Production Don’t stop at a working demo. Turn it into a system you can actually deploy. 20% off with code PROD20 until Apr 30 → Join the course Still copying text into ChatGPT like it\'s 2022? We\'re all drowning in tabs these days... Copying text from one place, pasting it into another, switching between tools just to write a simple message. It completely kills your flow. And that\'s where Clico comes in. This Chrome extension lives right inside your browser and understands the context of whatever you\'re reading or writing (no copying, no pasting, no tab-switching!). Summon it with a shortcut, use voice input, pull context from multiple tabs or get instant page summaries. It works everywhere you type: Gmail, Notion, Slack… you name it. It just hit number one on Product Hunt, it\'s free, and your privacy is protected. Try it The four prompting techniques to save Most LLM output is mediocre because most prompts are flat. The four techniques below fix the failure modes that hit most outputs in real use, and each one takes about 30 seconds to apply once you know it. Few-shot prompting: Show 2-5 input/output pairs and let the model copy the pattern. Best for classification, extraction and any task with a consistent format. Three good examples teach more than a 200-word instruction. Chain-of-thought: Ask the model to reason step by step before answering. Best for math, logic and multi-hop questions. Use it when you need to audit the reasoning, not just the output. Role-specific prompting: Skip \"act as an expert.\" Use \"senior fixed-income advisor with 20 years on the buy side.\" Specificity shifts vocabulary, depth and which knowledge the model surfaces. Negative prompting: Tell the model what to avoid in concrete terms. \"Do not invent statistics\" works because it names a specific failure mode. Best when you can point to a failure you\'ve actually seen. These four cover the failure modes that hit most LLM output. Run them as defaults and the same model gives you better answers without changing anything else. Most prompting advice in circulation is some version of these four, dressed up in different vocabulary. Five ways to cut your Claude Opus 4.7 token bill Anthropic kept the Opus 4.7 sticker price identical to 4.6 on launch day, but the new tokenizer inflates token counts by up to 35% on the same text, raising effective cost by that margin. The same release shipped five levers that pull the bill back down. Prompt caching: Send long, stable conversation history as a cached prefix. Cache hits cost 10% of the standard input price. Batch processing: Send Anthropic a list of prompts that don\'t need an instant answer and pay 50% less. Good for anything you can run overnight, like generating descriptions for 5,000 products or processing a week of customer feedback. Effort levels: Opus 4.7 ships with adjustable effort. Low-effort 4.7 is roughly equivalent to medium-effort 4.6. Step down a tier on tasks that don\'t need the maximum. Task budgets: Set hard caps on token consumption per run, now in public beta on the API. Stops a runaway loop from draining your budget without warning. Specify the task up front: Well-specified prompts in turn one (intent, constraints, acceptance criteria, file locations) beat ambiguous prompts that get clarified across many turns. Five levers, applied together, can cut your Opus 4.7 bill in half on the same workload. Caching is the highest-leverage move for any agent stack chaining context across multiple turns. The 35% tokenizer inflation only matters if you don\'t pull any of them. The 19 AI tools that cover the team you\'d otherwise hire Almost every role inside a small company now has an AI tool that does a serviceable version of the job. The stack below covers 19 categories across five clusters. Strategy & Ops: ChatGPT for strategy, Claude for writing, Perplexity for research, Rows for spreadsheets that pull live data and run AI inside the cells. Build & Automate: Replit for development, Webflow for production sites, Zapier for connecting everything to everything, Openclaw for repetitive computer tasks. Content & Design: Canva for brand assets, Gamma for decks from a prompt, Freepik for image and video, Veed for editing without Premiere. Growth & Distribution: Taplio for LinkedIn, Tweet Hunter for X, Sandcastles AI for Instagram, VidIQ for YouTube. Customer-Facing: Beehiiv for newsletters, HubSpot for CRM, Expertise AI for support tickets. Picking the tools is the easy part. Most teams stop there and end up with 19 demos that never see a real customer. Wiring tools into a system that handles errors and survives real volume is what GenAI Academy\'s From Demo to Production course was built to teach. Top AI courses of the week Claude Code Mastery. For engineers running Claude Code in production. The claude.md system, the 13-step ship-it workflow and reusable skills. Career Essentials in Generative AI. For any worker who needs a baseline understanding of generative AI without going deep. Free, around four hours. AI Governance Framework. For anyone whose legal team has started asking questions. A working AI compliance system in four weeks. ChatGPT Prompt Engineering for Developers. For developers using OpenAI API who want a tighter system around what works and why. Free, 1.5 hours. Vibe Coding with Python. Live four-week cohort starting May 12. For non-technical builders who want to ship real Python apps using ChatGPT, Claude or Gemini.\nKeep reading on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/how-keep-claude-from-wiping-production-backups-genai-works-lbuvf?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BokYddbSPSSaQRZYWI7GGVQ%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=1PpSr_Ev7X2sg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_-null-icq8ji~mokfd70v~ih-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mokfd70v-ih\n  \n      \n\n----------------------------------------\n\nThis email was intended for Yashica Lohar (Flipkart GWC 7.0 Scholar | CSE ’28 @ IIIT Jabalpur | 2 ⭐ @Codechef)\nLearn why we included this: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/4788?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BokYddbSPSSaQRZYWI7GGVQ%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=1PpSr_Ev7X2sg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mokfd70v~ih-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mokfd70v-ih\nYou are receiving Linke