vitation\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a871f4f7-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Atlas\n\nBy GenAI Works\n\n\nBy GenAI Works\n\n    \n    \n    Read this article on LinkedIn to join the conversation\nRead on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/why-anthropic-engineers-ditched-md-html-genai-works-3gfae?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3B1cXsM0tWTtC9Y6q2BlV5RA%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=0ktmpsRC67jsg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_-null-icq8ji~mp1kpcky~mx-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mp1kpcky-mx\n  \nWelcome back! Twenty HTML artifacts. That is what a Claude Code engineer at Anthropic posted last week as the evidence that markdown was the wrong default for AI agent output all along. Below the breakdown you\'ll also find the paper where five GPTs lifted GPT-4.1 by 49% just by talking to each other, plus OpenAI\'s enterprise leadership playbook. In today\'s Generative AI Newsletter: Anthropic: A Claude Code engineer makes the case that markdown was the wrong default for agent output. Ctx2Skill: Five GPTs in a feedback loop lifted GPT-4.1 by 49% on hard technical questions without fine-tuning. OpenAI: A five-step playbook distilled from working with hundreds of enterprises scaling AI. Why a Claude Code engineer ditched markdown for HTML Thariq Shihipar, who works on Claude Code at Anthropic, posted a thread last week arguing that HTML is the right default for AI agent output, not markdown. He backed it with twenty HTML artifacts side by side. His read is that markdown won by accident.  You can imagine how drastic this “accident” is when you remember that the core config files at the heart of Claude Code (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md and SKILL.md) are all markdown, so the agent inherited it as the default for everything it produces, including 200-line plans and code reviews nobody reads.  What makes HTML the winner is that it supports collapsible sections, internal links and interactive scaffolding, which is the difference between a plan you scroll past in fifteen seconds and a plan you actually act on. His thread is the clearest case yet that the markdown default is overdue for a rethink. Read the full article Have you built your first application with AI yet? The worst way to learn about AI is to read. It’s time to build your own applications.  Build real Python apps without memorizing syntax for months first. In Vibe Coding with Python, you describe what you want, AI generates the code and you guide, test and refine the result. In 4 weeks, you go from zero coding experience to real Python applications. Web apps, data dashboards and automation scripts, built with ChatGPT, Claude or any AI tool you choose. You learn a structured prompting framework, a systematic debugging workflow and a project-based approach that produces working software. By Week 4, you present a portfolio-ready capstone application you built yourself. Led by Paul Carlo Tordecilla. Starts May 12, PM PT. Last call enrollment is open with 20% off. Join the cohort How five GPTs talking to each other lifted GPT-4.1 by 49%? Take a frozen LLM, give it a dense technical document, and ask it difficult context-grounded questions. Normally, performance is weak because models struggle to extract reusable reasoning strategies from long technical contexts. What’s the solution to this? Having different GPTs discuss it with each other. Check the table below for a breakdown of the before and after. The idea here is simple. Instead of relying on external supervision, the system creates a multi-agent feedback loop where several GPT-style roles continuously challenge, evaluate, and refine one another. Over multiple iterations, the model effectively writes and updates its own “skill list” based on what it learns from failures and successes. What makes these numbers especially important is that there is no fine-tuning, no RLHF pipeline, no human labeling and no external feedback system. The improvement comes entirely from structured reasoning loops and iterative skill refinement.  This paper discusses the findings in full detail. And if you want to learn how to implement this 5 GPT system yourself, stay tuned for next week’s Technical Monday newsletter! 😉 One guide you can\'t miss this week OpenAI\'s enterprise team published a leadership playbook on what separates the companies that scale AI past pilot from the ones that spend money without an actual ROI.  It’s distilled from working with hundreds of large enterprises this year. OpenAI has access to all the data even their enterprise clients can see, so whenever they publish a guide, we’re all ears.  The framework runs five steps. Align, Activate, Amplify, Accelerate and Govern. Each comes with reflection questions you can run inside a leadership meeting without modification. Useful if you are the person inside a company who has to defend AI spend to a CFO this quarter. Download the guide THE AI BRIEFING: Agentic Fine-Tuning & Open Source Models with Ash Lewis Enterprise AI teams are looking for models that fit their workflows without adding complexity. On May 12 at 6 PM PST, join Steve Nouri and Ash Lewis, co-founder and CEO of Fastino Labs, for a conversation on Pioneer – an agent that fine-tunes open-source models using production data. Explore how open models are narrowing the gap with closed systems and what this means for AI ROI. Register now Light Bytes GM now turns a designer\'s sketch into a finished car animation in under a day, work that used to occupy three teams for months and the kind of compression Detroit needs to catch BYD. Microsoft CEO Satya Nadella has been subpoenaed in Elon Musk\'s OpenAI lawsuit, which puts Microsoft\'s role in the November 2023 board crisis back on a witness stand. The European Commission, author of the AI Act and chief sovereign-AI evangelist for two years, is choosing between US companies for its own internal AI with Mistral nowhere on the shortlist. Investors are pricing Alphabet to retake the most-valuable-company crown from Nvidia, two years after the same trade had Google written off as the AI loser. Greece is debating whether to add AI rights and obligations to its constitution, which would make it the first EU country to put model governance in a founding document. 📸 Check our Instagram for AI news in 30 seconds  🐝 Check our Beehiiv for the full daily rundown  📺 Check our YouTube to learn from the people building AI  🐦 Check ourX for AI news as it lands\nKeep reading on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/why-anthropic-engineers-ditched-md-html-genai-works-3gfae?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3B1cXsM0tWTtC9Y6q2BlV5RA%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=0ktmpsRC67jsg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_-null-icq8ji~mp1kpcky~mx-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mp1kpcky-mx\n  \n      \n\n----------------------------------------\n\nThis email was intended for Yashica Lohar (Flipkart GWC 7.0 Scholar | CSE ’28 @ IIIT Jabalpur | 2 ⭐ @Codechef)\nLearn why we included this: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/4788?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3B1cXsM0tWTtC9Y6q2BlV5RA%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=0ktmpsRC67jsg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mp1kpcky~mx-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mp1kpcky-mx\nYou are receiving LinkedIn notification emails. Others can see that you are a subscriber.\n\n\nUnsubscribe: https://www.linkedin.com/series-notifications/?action=unsubscribe&memberToken=ADoAAEIlwb4B7wSObgzu320aKxhPrfHhU2UtxwY&newsletterId=7075090904906149891&newsletterTitle=The Atlas&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3B1cXsM0tWTtC9Y6q2BlV5RA%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=0ktmpsRC67jsg1&ek=email_series_follow_newsletter_02&e=icq8ji-mp1kpcky-mx&eid=icq8ji-mp1kpcky-mx&m=unsubscribe&ts=footerGlimmer&li=0&t=plh    ·  Help: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/67?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3B1cXsM0tWTtC9Y6q2BlV5RA%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=0ktmpsRC67jsg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-help-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-help-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mp1kpcky~mx-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mp1kpcky-mx\n\n© 2026 LinkedIn Corporation, 1zwnj000 West Maude Avenue, Sunnyvale, CA 94085.\nLinkedIn and the LinkedIn logo are registered trademarks of LinkedIn.','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a872990f-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear The Atlas,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"Why Anthropic engineers ditched .md for HTML\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a8807a85-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'India Industry Insights\n\nBy Accenture in India\n\n\nBy Accenture in India\n\n    \n    \n    Read this article on LinkedIn to join the conversation\nRead on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/making-brands-unmissable-how-agents-reshaping-commerce-lxxuc?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3B8dzPr0OmSKq6xUlVZune0A%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=28jH-kvcr3jYg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_-null-icq8ji~mp259awm~ro-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mp259awm-ro\n  \nWhat if the next generation of an organization’s most valuable customers never visits their website, never sees their advertising and never consciously chooses their brand—because an AI agent chose it for them first? This is not too distant in the future. Agentic commerce is changing who makes purchasing decisions, when those decisions happen and on what basis they are made. This is the biggest shift in commerce in 20 years. The implications run through every function in an organization: marketing, supply chain, payments, operations, talent, etc. Put simply: We’re heading into a world where demand is shaped and captured inside agent-led journeys, not just human-led journeys. And all brands in all industries will be affected. Why the Current Commerce Model Is Failing For Accenture’s new report, Agentic Commerce: Make your Brand Unmissable, we partnered with Aaru—an AI behavior modeling firm—to run simulations of how agent-mediated commerce could evolve over the next two years. We combined those findings with Accenture’s broader consumer and executive research to arrive at insightful findings. Here is the uncomfortable starting point: the digital commerce model that organizations have spent the last decade perfecting has a fundamental structural flaw. Accenture research shows 85% of consumers, including in India, are likely to abandon an online purchase due to frustration or indecision. And three in four survey respondents feel overwhelmed by too many options. These are not fringe experiences—they are the norm. Agentic AI is filling a gap that the system itself created and never resolved. Across sectors and experiences like travel, banking, grocery, etc., agents are behaving like actors. People are still the customers. Winning requires being machine-readable, reliably available and operationally flawless—not merely persuasive. How Fast Agentic Commerce Is Scaling Based on the report, up to 45% of shoppers are expected to shift at least half of their commerce activities into agent-mediated ecosystems within the next two years. Within 18 to 24 months, a majority of customers will complete purchases in AI conversations that did not start with an explicit intent to buy. From our executive research—a survey of 4,000 executives conducted in January 2026—a quarter of executives already believe that in three years AI agents will be their number one audience for content, surpassing even search engines. How Agents Create Value and Shape Choice A useful way to identify where agentic solutions create the most value is to focus on the commerce mission—what consumers want to achieve—rather than channels or categories. For repeatable purchases like groceries, agents function as automated reordering engines, delivering value through smart substitutions and basket optimization. For lifestyle categories such as fashion and beauty, agents act as curators, using deep customer understanding to drive personalized recommendations, bundling, and discovery. In more complex purchases like travel, electronics, and financial products, agents become trusted advisors—simplifying trade-offs, modeling scenarios, and assembling end to end solutions. Across all missions, the differentiator is the quality and accessibility of a brand’s data and execution capability. What was once operational hygiene is now a decisive commercial advantage. Strategic Implications for Brands Two agent types are emerging. Horizontal agents are broad, general-purpose systems built for discovery and comparison across categories, helping consumers evaluate trade-offs early in the buying journey. Success with them depends on clear, current, well structured product data that AI can reliably assess. Vertical agents specialize within a category, using richer data and deeper integration to move faster from conversation to transaction—driving convenience and loyalty. Across both, the rule is simple: the closer you are to the agent making the purchase decision, the greater your influence on growth. Agentic commerce presents two strategic paths with distinct demands. Getting selected means optimizing for horizontal agents by being machine readable, operationally reliable, and easy to evaluate—clear pricing, verifiable claims, smooth transactions, and dependable fulfillment are table stakes. Going direct means building a category specific agent where you have real authority, powered by deep domain expertise, first party data, and end to end integration. The first is a baseline requirement for all; the second is a true advantage only if the foundations are firmly in place. The report outlines that Agentic commerce is as much a cost and margin play as a revenue one: By reducing abandonment, returns, fraud, and exceptions, it protects margins By enabling real time, demand driven supply chains and smarter payments, it turns operations into a profit lever By shifting to always on automation governed by skilled talent, it creates durable advantage—not just tech-led growth. The Moves that Matter for Brands Now Three moves matter for brands, both globally and in India, now: Show up for agents through GEO, aligned social–agent strategies, and KPI-led experiments Fix owned channels by making apps, sites, and stores agent ready and seamlessly connected Strengthen the foundation with accurate, machine-readable product data, policies, payments, and real time supply chains—because without that base, everything else underperforms. The brands that will be unmissable are those that start now. Read summary | Read detailed report | Discuss Accenture is ready to help as you begin to reimagine your business. If you’d like to know more about how we can partner with you in your Reinvention journey, please feel free to contact us. For careers in Consulting at Accenture, please visit our Careers Portal.\nKeep reading on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/making-brands-unmissable-how-agents-reshaping-commerce-lxxuc?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3B8dzPr0OmSKq6xUlVZune0A%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=28jH-kvcr3jYg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_-null-icq8ji~mp259awm~ro-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mp259awm-ro\n  \n      \n\n----------------------------------------\n\nThis email was intended for Yashica Lohar (Flipkart GWC 7.0 Scholar | CSE ’28 @ IIIT Jabalpur | 2 ⭐ @Codechef)\nLearn why we included this: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/4788?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3B8dzPr0OmSKq6xUlVZune0A%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=28jH-kvcr3jYg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mp259awm~ro-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mp259awm-ro\nYou are receiving LinkedIn notification emails. Others can see that you are a subscriber.\n\n\nUnsubscribe: https://www.linkedin.com/series-notifications/?action=unsubscribe&memberToken=ADoAAEIlwb4B7wSObgzu320aKxhPrfHhU2UtxwY&newsletterId=6930730011909910528&newsletterTitle=India Industry Insights&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3B8dzPr0OmSKq6xUlVZune0A%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=28jH-kvcr3jYg1&ek=email_series_follow_newsletter_02&e=icq8ji-mp259awm-ro&eid=icq8ji-mp259awm-ro&m=unsubscribe&ts=footerGlimmer&li=0&t=plh    ·  Help: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/67?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3B8dzPr0OmSKq6xUlVZune0A%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=28jH-kvcr3jYg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-help-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-help-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mp259awm~ro-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mp259awm-ro\n\n© 2026 LinkedIn Corporation, 1zwnj000 West Maude Avenue, Sunnyvale, CA 94085.\nLinkedIn and the LinkedIn logo are registered trademarks of LinkedIn.','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a88113f6-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear India Industry Insights,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"Making Brands ‘Unmissable’: How Agents are reshaping Commerce and Customer Relationships\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a888b90e-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Have a closer look at our latest climate milestone\n\nCanva  ( https://l.engage.canva.com/ss/c/u001.Note3it1gaozj0PIggVG9tplar3juom3GwdJknmjC21LPkKYtHz0x6QJatPek3qG/4qk/DXqwHxTtQ4GvlODRrnA7zQ/t0/h001.uJiL6z9h_Y_yO6FHayMcAzx97ckHJcPs_bkN8J0zmaY )\nPro           Canva  \n( https://l.engage.canva.com/ss/c/u001.Note3it1gaozj0PIggVG9tplar3juom3GwdJknmjC21MTfEPyErKQLyixV7WzUwm/4qk/DXqwHxTtQ4GvlODRrnA7zQ/t1/h001.d9hPHN_99ZNaY4x18yrHESpefvt7vxYlNEVkK2PMOAE )\n    \n( https://l.engage.canva.com/ss/c/u001.Note3it1gaozj0PIggVG9jSYjQmDyWZrqxUXjHgaLPLrZ8tIb_ozLBO7iNkCjuk7u8v3ndXBmFTNN9lyll-yZOx71c1LFXnD_h7YWq5nHYlQzMbbtOojki86u-ymxsYH/4qk/DXqwHxTtQ4GvlODRrnA7zQ/t2/h001.pjqdU2Nf6JUQXVdGYfb5IdWg5eDZlwlqmSGOLcFv5E4 )\n         \n( https://l.engage.canva.com/ss/c/u001.Note3it1gaozj0PIggVG9tplar3juom3GwdJknmjC20nVSNE54r17iGvom2qMRDx/4qk/DXqwHxTtQ4GvlODRrnA7zQ/t3/h001.cQCKEVOXU0k2rSpBX2xSNeu9dDzvxgDcRIITisLHyxs )\nPicture of opening of the solar farm, co-funded by Canva \n( https://l.engage.canva.com/ss/c/u001.Note3it1gaozj0PIggVG9riuMQOiWXvCs0zKBsfUSI4E-e9TC9QsU3sAKHYn9icdcVvOO8NcUutvZ8iBRfqDbEBoanYnaqJ_V28TuQRhAb4/4qk/DXqwHxTtQ4GvlODRrnA7zQ/t4/h001.Nr3BWShQOsqWjpjwPipPw4ofLGGhzi2fe4fhiJ6n_kY )\n\n\n******************\nPowered by the sun\n\n******************\n\nWe’re now generating enough renewable electricity to match what\ngoes into every Canva print order across the US and Canada. A\nstep closer to net zero by 2040, made possible together with our\npartners.\n\nCurious how it all works? Dive into the full story behind the\nsolar farms and the impact they\'re designed to create.\n\nRead the story  \n( https://l.engage.canva.com/ss/c/u001.Note3it1gaozj0PIggVG9riuMQOiWXvCs0zKBsfUSI4E-e9TC9QsU3sAKHYn9icdcVvOO8NcUutvZ8iBRfqDbLvuXax33-Np-QgJoNM57KI/4qk/DXqwHxTtQ4GvlODRrnA7zQ/t5/h001.AuCAePOCXmaL3m91LMz8E0mdveNRvGx-RW_dISxup98 )\n A\nquote from Cameron Adams on how Canva is building a better energy\ngrid \n( https://l.engage.canva.com/ss/c/u001.Note3it1gaozj0PIggVG9riuMQOiWXvCs0zKBsfUSI4E-e9TC9QsU3sAKHYn9icdcVvOO8NcUutvZ8iBRfqDbHIQkJbmr4xd3PqgsZNtPC4/4qk/DXqwHxTtQ4GvlODRrnA7zQ/t6/h001.Nioeb6N92URRXz30ptI85iTCLMMc_ndE9RoBFCP7f1c )\n\n\n***************\nBetter together\n***************\n\nOur US and Canadian Print partners have committed to Canva\'s\nClimate Commitment, measuring and matching their electricity use\nwith renewable energy. It\'s a shared way to cut emissions while\nhelping fund new clean energy where the grid needs it most.\n\nTake a closer look at how the commitment works.\n\nExplore the commitment  \n( https://l.engage.canva.com/ss/c/u001.ubsHQYUcS4c6b2aqjEPpSzEL2ZTCUjgxUxvr0SadCPwq7upwnKhnoD8phFpBqtOCnOTF0Y2QUORLFxbOsBE0M8xlHpg_Fbdk8oBqOfF5mFU/4qk/DXqwHxTtQ4GvlODRrnA7zQ/t7/h001.ftauMp6uYP5uR5tehhF7bijqLT0M3n1PxaLC2KG3xD8 )\n\n\n\n \n( https://l.engage.canva.com/ss/c/u001.Note3it1gaozj0PIggVG9inNSLfUvwU6C00u-AIKuxJS6ju0jjpJ67_tQDH4JJfT7S8Ulo2P_EpckQ2MEKPWoQ/4qk/DXqwHxTtQ4GvlODRrnA7zQ/t8/h001.ungVo-cgJbyKruQhtpAe5YhGlhaXev2Ql7mQOJNRbyA )\n \n( https://l.engage.canva.com/ss/c/u001.Note3it1gaozj0PIggVG9inNSLfUvwU6C00u-AIKuxLF5Iyal_3ep0m0gr2Zwx6-is2RWV0Ps57-9sxJOsvP7g/4qk/DXqwHxTtQ4GvlODRrnA7zQ/t9/h001.pHteEpl-5BSsGwq76SXBQ1F3OxgMLHi3cqmyN6zmoyI )\n \n( https://l.engage.canva.com/ss/c/u001.Note3it1gaozj0PIggVG9inNSLfUvwU6C00u-AIKuxJ0huWxsBizj11xBs5Tf8pzgCvXRsmNPPJuS9SdIbjspw/4qk/DXqwHxTtQ4GvlODRrnA7zQ/t10/h001.Ec_dA44OrjKtnFp-g07qR-cmgLKsiRE37fr8QT8ZOcE )\n \n( https://l.engage.canva.com/ss/c/u001.Note3it1gaozj0PIggVG9inNSLfUvwU6C00u-AIKuxIUhCbjNKrLo1zkeVFC5nHuuyoNOeW9oimYjH1AV-EFqA/4qk/DXqwHxTtQ4GvlODRrnA7zQ/t11/h001.oqJn5JPimDNLhRaggRRIeItxZiWKs6lpWXxlRHpTsR0 )\n \n( https://l.engage.canva.com/ss/c/u001.Note3it1gaozj0PIggVG9inNSLfUvwU6C00u-AIKuxIgwxa6pVAlidlWdrQ6dk-MpyoqisrClBN3hvm8FX_17A/4qk/DXqwHxTtQ4GvlODRrnA7zQ/t12/h001.csG20iBHO5_PkIRPZM5ec3NrybAj8uYlpl_K_34oejQ )\n       app store \n( https://l.engage.canva.com/ss/c/u001.Note3it1gaozj0PIggVG9tplar3juom3GwdJknmjC20nuEYEticUPDxc00LYp82f/4qk/DXqwHxTtQ4GvlODRrnA7zQ/t13/h001._zZ6UOOH06sklm1SSNqyORgoE4_iKZ6eQRORBnX9mkY )    google play \n( https://l.engage.canva.com/ss/c/u001.Note3it1gaozj0PIggVG9tplar3juom3GwdJknmjC21NSrZvA9QL5LiIPPYjyb5Y/4qk/DXqwHxTtQ4GvlODRrnA7zQ/t14/h001.XPUrjgyNsU83YBDGMFxLikjtInhxS3U6jfu-tjXvNs0 )\n\n\nCanva Pty Ltd, 110 Kippax St, Sydney, NSW 2010, Australia. ABN\n80 158 929 938\n\n \n( https://l.engage.canva.com/ss/c/u001.Note3it1gaozj0PIggVG9tplar3juom3GwdJknmjC232B1kjw2C2HAdyFrKxkYGe/4qk/DXqwHxTtQ4GvlODRrnA7zQ/t15/h001.PQ1mQ-qgIJkD-RkQbFmAFMzvhf8jdjfHA3iuM5traYA )\n \n( https://l.engage.canva.com/ss/c/u001.Note3it1gaozj0PIggVG9tIXV7HLfu7ev9kt5wgj4xCOUuEGJuAJL8PEwDynpvWHv8tFBkZLkmtt2VlWMzDZITXdaojgKxZflSwNHLGIbjduq2ryCz20BNxAv8jBf1wD/4qk/DXqwHxTtQ4GvlODRrnA7zQ/t16/h001.gM3GXpIUcQLtd0jsA5lY6jwRe0hKxSq2hJEBepLHcEA )\n           \n( https://l.engage.canva.com/ss/c/u001.Note3it1gaozj0PIggVG9t1o6OOPWBTK2sz3h-0nOIbQyLvBmKKHsNPdhh_PATD2KZcF5nI3jxpsieDv1o5Dv5yBgw4lmm6iBXr0wvV_KzY/4qk/DXqwHxTtQ4GvlODRrnA7zQ/t17/h001.wf6jUa30H48LZHmQziP8lvZOpl4Gtqn4-OkxQjAD0wg )\n       Datenschutz \n( https://l.engage.canva.com/ss/c/u001.Note3it1gaozj0PIggVG9hFQIAv