28 @ IIIT Jabalpur | 2 ⭐ @Codechef)\nLearn why we included this: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/4788?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_weekly_analytics_recap_v2%3BvNQW%2F9vwRUyqx%2BbZw61JTg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=32NAEOmvMAkcg1&trk=eml-email_weekly_analytics_recap_v2-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_weekly_analytics_recap_v2-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mp291edl~rc-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mp291edl-rc\nYou are receiving LinkedIn notification emails.\n\n\nUnsubscribe: https://www.linkedin.com/comm/psettings/email-unsubscribe?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_weekly_analytics_recap_v2%3BvNQW%2F9vwRUyqx%2BbZw61JTg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=32NAEOmvMAkcg1&trk=eml-email_weekly_analytics_recap_v2-unsubscribe-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_weekly_analytics_recap_v2-unsubscribe-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mp291edl~rc-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mp291edl-rc&loid=AQF0e4k0TsG4aAAAAZ4a3wCngHPlynXkG84L6V4TTEk5ONz-ylHdoW2gJudjYQr4BaP8H45j4KnP5Jd895QLzcTsbL7QudkZ9ti3js20X5qcAHEyZsqGvDU\nHelp: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/67?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_weekly_analytics_recap_v2%3BvNQW%2F9vwRUyqx%2BbZw61JTg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=32NAEOmvMAkcg1&trk=eml-email_weekly_analytics_recap_v2-help-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_weekly_analytics_recap_v2-help-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mp291edl~rc-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mp291edl-rc\n\n© 2026 LinkedIn Corporation, 1zwnj000 West Maude Avenue, Sunnyvale, CA 94085.\nLinkedIn and the LinkedIn logo are registered trademarks of LinkedIn.','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a88e9416-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear LinkedIn,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"Yashica, your posts got 32 impressions last week\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a8942bbe-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Zoho Bulletin\n\nBy Zoho\n\n\nBy Zoho\n\n    \n    \n    Read this article on LinkedIn to join the conversation\nRead on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/we-may-have-lot-share-month-zoho-eqdxc?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BtziN4MVqQJmgzuBp50RopA%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=3klSnFY3t8kcg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_-null-icq8ji~mp2a2088~46-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mp2a2088-46\n  \nHello and welcome back to another edition of the Bulletin. This month, we have some thoughtful reads on AI, partner training worth looking back on, and a few stories that are just good to sit with. So let\'s get to it! What AI research taught our head of AI security about life 🌱 Sujatha S Iyer, our head of AI security, joined us as an intern over a decade ago, drawn in by the idea that an algorithm could understand how someone was feeling from the way they wrote. That curiosity led her down the path of AI, machine learning, and NLP—and eventually to building one of the most robust AI cyber-defense ecosystems in the industry. In this piece, she reflects on the journey with rare honesty—on experimentation as a career strategy, on the particular weight of self-doubt that many women in tech carry, and on why the logic of AI research turns out to be surprisingly good life advice. If you’ve ever wondered whether you’re on the right path, this one’s worth a read. New Apple device for the business? We brought company. 😎 Zoho blister packs for Bigin by Zoho CRM, Zoho Books, and Zoho Workplace are now available at select Apple Authorized Partners across India—so you can walk out with not just a new device, but the software you need to run your business too. A few days in the mountains with our partners in Japan 😇 Earlier this month, we headed to Kawane, Shizuoka: a quiet mountain town that turned out to be the perfect backdrop for Partner training that felt like so much more. Between product deep-dives, shared Indian meals, and time spent with the local community, some of the best conversations happened nowhere near a slide deck. We’re grateful to all the partners who made the trip—they were days well spent! The desk diaries 💚 You know how a desk eventually becomes an extension of your personality? We thought it’d be fun to spotlight a few around here. First up: Anusha Muralidharan, who heads enterprise and partner marketing in India. One look at her workspace tells you everything—books stacked with intention, a carefully curated collection of miniatures, and a very clear commitment to the color green. We see you, Anusha! Keep an eye out: More desks and more personalities are coming soon. Leadership lessons from a 2,000-year-old Tamil text Here’s something you don’t read every day: a piece of writing composed over two millennia ago, translated into more than 60 languages, quoted by Tolstoy, and—as it turns out—remarkably applicable to running a modern business. The Thirukkural, authored by Valluvar in Tamil, is a collection of 1,330 couplets covering everything from ethics to diplomacy to the art of not being a terrible boss. Our team curated 10 specifically for leaders, grouped into three themes: the qualities worth cultivating, how to pick the right people, and the traps that quietly undo even capable leaders. One of our favorites: “A leader with no one to criticize them will be ruined even with no saboteurs around.”  This one is worth a read, whether you’re managing a team of two or two thousand! From the horse\'s mouth AI makes coding cheaper. But that doesn’t make software less valuable. Everyone’s talking about how fast software can be built now. Far fewer are thinking about what happens when it actually has to hold up at scale, under pressure, and when things don’t go as planned. Ramprakash Ramamoorthy, director of AI research at Zoho, makes a distinction that’s easy to miss in all the noise: what AI makes cheaper is code production. What it doesn’t make cheaper is software ownership—the security, uptime, compliance, governance, and accountability that enterprise customers actually buy. If AI makes programming cheaper, it does not automatically make software less valuable. What becomes cheaper is code production. What does not become cheaper is software ownership. As he puts it, as code becomes cheaper, confidence becomes more valuable. It’s a grounded, well-argued read at a time when the headlines can get a little breathless. And that’s a wrap 👋 For everything happening across Zoho’s product universe, don’t forget to subscribe to Zoho Buzz—it’s the best way to keep up. And, as always, we’d love to know what you’d like to see more of, so let us know in the comments. See you in the next one!\nKeep reading on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/we-may-have-lot-share-month-zoho-eqdxc?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BtziN4MVqQJmgzuBp50RopA%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=3klSnFY3t8kcg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_-null-icq8ji~mp2a2088~46-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mp2a2088-46\n  \n      \n\n----------------------------------------\n\nThis email was intended for Yashica Lohar (Flipkart GWC 7.0 Scholar | CSE ’28 @ IIIT Jabalpur | 2 ⭐ @Codechef)\nLearn why we included this: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/4788?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BtziN4MVqQJmgzuBp50RopA%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=3klSnFY3t8kcg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mp2a2088~46-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mp2a2088-46\nYou are receiving LinkedIn notification emails. Others can see that you are a subscriber.\n\n\nUnsubscribe: https://www.linkedin.com/series-notifications/?action=unsubscribe&memberToken=ADoAAEIlwb4B7wSObgzu320aKxhPrfHhU2UtxwY&newsletterId=7041659773024428032&newsletterTitle=The Zoho Bulletin&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BtziN4MVqQJmgzuBp50RopA%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=3klSnFY3t8kcg1&ek=email_series_follow_newsletter_02&e=icq8ji-mp2a2088-46&eid=icq8ji-mp2a2088-46&m=unsubscribe&ts=footerGlimmer&li=0&t=plh    ·  Help: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/67?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BtziN4MVqQJmgzuBp50RopA%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=3klSnFY3t8kcg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-help-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-help-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mp2a2088~46-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mp2a2088-46\n\n© 2026 LinkedIn Corporation, 1zwnj000 West Maude Avenue, Sunnyvale, CA 94085.\nLinkedIn and the LinkedIn logo are registered trademarks of LinkedIn.','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a894d3d5-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear The Zoho Bulletin,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"We \'May\' have a lot to share this month 😉\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a8a27fd3-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Podcasting Made Simple\n\nBy Alex Sanfilippo\n\n\nBy Alex Sanfilippo\n\n    \n    \n    Read this article on LinkedIn to join the conversation\nRead on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/how-make-lasting-impression-podcast-guest-alex-sanfilippo-cjuxe?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3B7lKjwr3yTQqnmD8ZorFLPg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=2IRgO0V9akksg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_-null-icq8ji~mp2lzirw~qm-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mp2lzirw-qm\n  \nMost podcast guests wing it. They end up oversharing and have no direction for where the conversation is heading. Thankfully, there’s a better way to be an effective podcast guest! In this episode, Dianne Wilson shares a simple 3-step approach to ensure you’re prepared and have proper direction when you’re in the podcast guest seat. Get ready to nail your next interview so hosts and listeners remember you for years to come! 🎧 Watch or Listen to This Episode of Podcasting Made Simple: https://PodMatch.com/Episodes (Then Search \"383\") 📝 Big Ideas From This Episode: 1. Lead with conviction Confidence is a credibility signal. People remember how you say it. Use steady tone, energy, and conviction so listeners trust you fast, even before details. 2. Be the green light Do not wait for applause to speak with confidence. Choose to belong before proof shows up. Lead with conviction even when it feels uncomfortable. 3. Treat it like a performance A guest spot is not a casual coffee chat. Show up with a plan for impact. Know your message, your 2 to 3 best stories, and the point you will land at the end. 4. Master your story out loud Practice your story out loud so it stays clear under pressure. When you know the beats, you can adapt live without rambling or sounding scripted. 5. Be relevant, not just relatable Relatable can make people like you, but relevance makes them remember you. Tie every story to the listener’s problem and the result they want next. Attend Podcasting Made Simple Live For Free by visiting https://PodMatch.com/event and use code PMLIVE! 6. Ask 3 intent questions Before the interview ask: what do I want to be known for. What does this audience care about. What part of my story helps them while they half listen. 7. Avoid the stall When asked tell us about yourself, skip the long warmup and disclaimers. Give one clean thread: who you help, why it matters, and the turning point. 8. Make them see themselves Before listeners trust your expertise, they need to see themselves in you. Use specific stakes, a clear pivot, and the lesson that changed your actions. 9. Win the first five minutes The first five minutes can make the moment. Open with intention, earn attention fast, and plant a clear takeaway early so the rest of the talk lands. 💡 Final Thought: A lasting impression is rarely about having the perfect script. It is about showing up with intention, telling your story with conviction, and making it useful for the listener. When hosts and guests treat the conversation with care, the episode feels grounded and memorable. The best opportunities usually come from the relationships formed in moments like these, long after the recording ends. 💬 Did you listen to or watch this episode of Podcasting Made Simple? If yes, what was your biggest takeaway?\nKeep reading on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/how-make-lasting-impression-podcast-guest-alex-sanfilippo-cjuxe?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3B7lKjwr3yTQqnmD8ZorFLPg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=2IRgO0V9akksg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_-null-icq8ji~mp2lzirw~qm-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mp2lzirw-qm\n  \n      \n\n----------------------------------------\n\nThis email was intended for Yashica Lohar (Flipkart GWC 7.0 Scholar | CSE ’28 @ IIIT Jabalpur | 2 ⭐ @Codechef)\nLearn why we included this: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/4788?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3B7lKjwr3yTQqnmD8ZorFLPg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=2IRgO0V9akksg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mp2lzirw~qm-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mp2lzirw-qm\nYou are receiving LinkedIn notification emails. Others can see that you are a subscriber.\n\n\nUnsubscribe: https://www.linkedin.com/series-notifications/?action=unsubscribe&memberToken=ADoAAEIlwb4B7wSObgzu320aKxhPrfHhU2UtxwY&newsletterId=7069288237738942464&newsletterTitle=Podcasting Made Simple&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3B7lKjwr3yTQqnmD8ZorFLPg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=2IRgO0V9akksg1&ek=email_series_follow_newsletter_02&e=icq8ji-mp2lzirw-qm&eid=icq8ji-mp2lzirw-qm&m=unsubscribe&ts=footerGlimmer&li=0&t=plh    ·  Help: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/67?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3B7lKjwr3yTQqnmD8ZorFLPg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=2IRgO0V9akksg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-help-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-help-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mp2lzirw~qm-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mp2lzirw-qm\n\n© 2026 LinkedIn Corporation, 1zwnj000 West Maude Avenue, Sunnyvale, CA 94085.\nLinkedIn and the LinkedIn logo are registered trademarks of LinkedIn.','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a8a319c0-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear Podcasting Made Simple,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"How to Make a Lasting Impression as a Podcast Guest\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('a8a82f4f-6633-11f1-bb83-60