t of AlgoQueen 2026, participants will also receive access to 10+ upcoming expert sessions featuring industry professionals, mentors, and experienced programmers.\n📲 Follow our official social media page for updates and announcements:\n@icpc_amrita_ on Instagram<https://www.instagram.com/icpc_amrita_/?utm_source=chatgpt.com>\n👉 Event Registration & Details:\nICPC AlgoQueen 2026 Official Website<https://algoqueen.icpc.global/?utm_source=chatgpt.com>\nFor any queries, feel free to contact us at algoqueen@cb.amrita.edu<mailto:algoqueen@cb.amrita.edu>.\nWe look forward to seeing you at the session! 🚀\nBest regards,\nICPC AlgoQueen Team 2026\nAmrita Vishwa Vidyapeetham | ICPC Foundation\n[Amrita University]\nDisclaimer: The information transmitted in this email, including attachments, is intended only for the person(s) or entity to which it is addressed and may contain confidential and/or privileged material. Any review, retransmission, dissemination or other use of, or taking of any action in reliance upon this information by persons or entities other than the intended recipient is prohibited. Any views expressed in any message are those of the individual sender and may not necessarily reflect the views of Amrita Vishwa Vidyapeetham. If you received this in error, please contact the sender and destroy any copies of this information.\n','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('abb1ae94-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear ICPC Amritapuri,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"Exclusive Speaker Session on DSA & Competitive Programming – ICPC AlgoQueen 2026.\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('abbfded0-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Podcasting Made Simple\n\nBy Alex Sanfilippo\n\n\nBy Alex Sanfilippo\n\n    \n    \n    Read this article on LinkedIn to join the conversation\nRead on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/podcast-guesting-builds-relationships-revenue-alex-sanfilippo-tecge?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BBgMGu%2BVxQDyD55R2EGdRgw%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=2xrY3qK3tJEcg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_-null-icq8ji~mpmn9u8a~c-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mpmn9u8a-c\n  \nAlgorithms change, and trends come and go; visibility alone puts you in a race that will never end. But, real relationships keep your business alive no matter what’s happening around you! In this episode, Rachel Allen shares how to treat podcast guesting like relationship-building, so you can earn trust and build connections over time. Get ready to build lasting relationships that will stand the test of time! 🎧 Watch or Listen to This Episode of Podcasting Made Simple: https://PodMatch.com/Episodes (Then Search \"385\") 📝 Big Ideas From This Episode: 1. Be heard, not loud Stop chasing visibility. Guest to be heard by the right people, build trust in 30 minutes, and step out of the endless social media arms race. 2. Pitch like a partner Hosts and guests: pitch like a partner. Personalize, keep it tight, and include 2 to 3 topic angles plus proof of results. Make the fit obvious in one scan. 3. Build the relationship in the pitch Add value in the pitch. Share a resource, connection, or insight that helps their audience now. Relationship first, booking second, so they remember you. 4. Prepare hard, then drop the script Hosts and guests: prepare hard, then drop the script. Know your stories and data, then talk like a human. Great episodes come from presence and play, not notes. 5. Collaborate in real time Hosts and guests: collaborate in real time. Listen for emotion and pivots, ask what happened next, and land the lesson for listeners, without hijacking. Attend Podcasting Made Simple Live For Free by visiting https://PodMatch.com/event and use code PMLIVE! 6. Follow up on a schedule Follow up like you mean it. Thank them right after, message on release, then set a 90 day check in. Offer help and keep the relationship alive. 7. Invite listeners into dialogue Make it easy for listeners to connect. Give one clear next step, share a direct contact path, then reply personally to every message you can. 8. Track the relationship flywheel Keep a relationship ledger. Track hosts, listeners, and warm contacts. Guesting becomes referrals and revenue when trust compounds over time. 9. Choose humanity on purpose Choose humanity on purpose. Show up real, useful, and curious. It is the one advantage platforms cannot copy, automate, or take away, in any economy. 💡 Final Thought: Podcast guesting works best when you treat it like relationship building, not marketing noise. A thoughtful pitch, a real conversation, and consistent follow up turn one episode into years of trust. That trust becomes referrals, partnerships, and sales because people remember how you showed up. In a world full of tactics, being human is still the move that lasts. 💬 Did you listen to or watch this episode of Podcasting Made Simple? If yes, what was your biggest takeaway?\nKeep reading on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/podcast-guesting-builds-relationships-revenue-alex-sanfilippo-tecge?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BBgMGu%2BVxQDyD55R2EGdRgw%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=2xrY3qK3tJEcg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_-null-icq8ji~mpmn9u8a~c-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mpmn9u8a-c\n  \n      \n\n----------------------------------------\n\nThis email was intended for Yashica Lohar (Flipkart GWC 7.0 S