G-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=1h9hOQ_NRyEsg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_-null-icq8ji~mpmvy9q0~vb-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mpmvy9q0-vb\n  \nIn math class, “show your work” felt like a punishment. Looking back, it seems like Mrs. Greenberg could see the future. Today, AI can generate content in seconds. But just because sales forecasts, marketing emails, and service resolutions can be served up easily, doesn\'t mean they\'re always correct. Making AI trustworthy still falls on us. That\'s what this issue is all about: AI performance reviews, when to hand the wheel back to a human, and how to measure success beyond the obvious metrics. So there were lessons in math class that apply to real life. That’s why we’ve re-memorized the quadratic formula. You never know when a customer will ask about it. Teddy\'s great. Theodore\'s on a PIP. Teddy never sleeps, is great at taking direction, and handles more than a thousand sales leads a week. He\'s an AI agent at Asymbl who\'s held to the same standard as human employees, with clear KPIs and honest feedback. When he does well, everyone\'s happy. When he drops the ball? They call him Theodore Frank and put him on a PIP. Accountability. It\'s not just for humans. Here you come to save the day When AI goes rogue in the movies it can lead to nuclear meltdowns or country-wide blackouts. At a small business, it looks more like hallucinated Q2 projections and off-brand marketing emails. That kind of storyline makes for boring sci-fi thrillers but high drama at the office. The hero who swoops in at just the right time won\'t be a cyborg. It\'ll be you. Here\'s when to step in. 525,600 metrics How do you measure success in customer service? The usual suspects include cost per contact, average handle time, and deflection rate but the growth of AI in service organizations has shifted expectations for both customers and employees. The metrics should shift too. Do your customers feel heard? Do your reps end the day feeling capable instead of burnt out? These stats are harder to quantify, but they\'re more measurable than you think. We’ve got some suggestions. This newsletter was curated by Benny Spiewak, Senior Marketing Lead at Salesforce.\nKeep reading on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/what-companies-can-learn-from-4th-grade-math-class-salesforce-hv7ac?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BN0YuMn3OQI6JFvbcBApS6A%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=1h9hOQ_NRyEsg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_-null-icq8ji~mpmvy9q0~vb-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mpmvy9q0-vb\n  \n      \n\n----------------------------------------\n\nThis email was intended for Yashica Lohar (Flipkart GWC 7.0 Scholar | CSE ’28 @ IIIT Jabalpur | 2 ⭐ @Codechef)\nLearn why we included this: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/4788?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BN0YuMn3OQI6JFvbcBApS6A%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=1h9hOQ_NRyEsg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mpmvy9q0~vb-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mpmvy9q0-vb\nYou are receiving LinkedIn notification emails. Others can see that you are a subscriber.\n\n\nUnsubscribe: https://www.linkedin.com/series-notifications/?action=unsubscribe&memberToken=ADoAAEIlwb4B7wSObgzu320aKxhPrfHhU2UtxwY&newsletterId=7079504890934263808&newsletterTitle=Do More With AI&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BN0YuMn3OQI6JFvbcBApS6A%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=1h9hOQ_NRyEsg1&ek=email_series_follow_newsletter_02&e=icq8ji-mpmvy9q0-vb&eid=icq8ji-mpmvy9q0-vb&m=unsubscribe&ts=footerGlimmer&li=0&t=plh    · 