t/api/utilities/v1/imageproxy/https://coursera-misc.s3.amazonaws.com/mailspin/prod/03_30_2023_18_59_36_icon-tik-tok.png]https://link.coursera.org/f/a/1qdqTgbuzJOfEQDtfiI3Tw~~/AAQRxRA~/ysoiOgXFot2m9oDnvrh0Wx4IhTc5ZOzqt9825iT1biKlt3YQ8y5_3j5MNhnoEuNLetLFe_E6a1GpPqOCbRj1Q9fZfF4YgN6Wm-nUn3B7CjwoFjIBdGc8W4Q4pHwYBfU7Tuh1TNwihNO-lcSxmfF-Kgxxo4wS3C9EeS8fjgpqhiLBBzhEEgSAowFewEdEB4ERJLTzRNyP6aUPT8qvB5DC_2jxtwoariTKa9kvqfVR8HfkI403qDBe1fqHuZqVQc50uoD646vl8tkAKS1fXGIGBwzQYf21NQ93whenqEKVt2LYgNp_oGV5wveCrPlRYi1a\n\n© 2026 Coursera Inc. All rights reserved. Coursera and the Coursera logo are\nregistered trademarks of Coursera, Inc. All other trademarks are property of\ntheir respective owners.\n\nCoursera | 2440 W El Camino Real 5th floor, Mountain View, CA 94040 USA\n\n                                                                   ','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('aca98633-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear Coursera,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"Your special-access series is inside!\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('acb1055e-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Atlas\n\nBy GenAI Works\n\n\nBy GenAI Works\n\n    \n    \n    Read this article on LinkedIn to join the conversation\nRead on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/claude-just-changed-economics-enterprise-ai-genai-works-1xvhe?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BNje0ToPWTBukh0ARwdk%2BTQ%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=2by5L5KGM9IIg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_-null-icq8ji~mpr4a9hp~g3-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mpr4a9hp-g3\n  \nWelcome back! This week, the new question is: What happens when AI starts doing the work? Anthropic answered that with Claude\'s new Dynamic Workflows feature. At the same time, Anthropic published a practical playbook showing how financial services firms are already using Claude across different operations. Google DeepMind attacked a different bottleneck: knowledge access. Gemini Embedding 2 promises to make digital assets searchable through a single retrieval layer, reducing both AI costs and operational complexity. And while companies race to deploy AI, China reminded the industry that infrastructure still matters. Beijing effectively closed one of Nvidia\'s remaining doors in China, redirecting future AI spending toward domestic suppliers. In today\'s Atlas Newsletter: Dynamic Workflows: How can Claude help your team finish projects in days instead of months? Finance teams & Claude: Six ways financial services firms are accelerating their most time-consuming work. China bans Nvidia: Why did Beijing redirect hundreds of millions in AI chip spending toward domestic suppliers? Gemini Embedding 2: How is Google reducing the cost and complexity of enterprise AI search? PS: Want to share your AI tool or company news with our 14M+ community? Get in touch. How can Claude help you finish your projects in days instead of months? If your enterprise is struggling with a backlog of technical work that never seems to move fast enough, you might consider Claude Dynamic Workflows. The idea behind this feature is simple. Instead of one AI agent working through a task step by step, Dynamic Workflows launches tens or even hundreds of parallel subagents. Some execute the work. Others review it, challenge assumptions, and look for errors. The rest verify the results before they are returned. The process runs continuously, saves progress automatically, and resumes exactly where it stopped if interrupted. For CTOs and engineering leaders, the economics are becoming difficult to ignore. Projects that once required large teams and multi-month timelines can now be completed faster, at lower cost, and with less disruption to ongoing work. The bottleneck has moved from team capacity to deciding which problem to solve first. What\'s most interesting is that, in one of our previous editions, we predicted that Claude would soon launch a Dynamic Workflows feature. Subscribe to read a deep analysis on how to use Claude\'s dynamic workflows feature here. Don\'t miss it. And if today\'s content feels a bit too advanced, GenAI Academy offers practical, hands-on courses designed to help professionals understand and apply the latest AI technologies.  We spent 800 hours learning Claude. You\'ll need 16 Anthropic ships new Claude features almost every week: Skills, Connectors, Cowork, vibe coding. The pace is hard to keep up with, and most people are still using Claude for basic chat. Our 2-Day Claude AI Mastery Workshop condenses 800+ hours of research, documentation, and real-world testing into a 16-hour live curriculum.  You\'ll learn Claude\'s three modes (Chat, Cowork, Code), set up Skills and Connectors to automate Notion, files, and desktop work, and vibe code your own dashboards alongside 10+ tools that pair with Claude. Saturday and Sunday, 10 AM to 7 PM EST. Free for the next 48 hours. Register free How are financial services firms accelerating work with Claude? If your financial services firm is struggling with time-consuming workflows that slow down operations, you might consider these six Claude best practices. Anthropic\'s latest financial services deployment guide shows what that looks like in practice: → An equity analyst uploads an earnings-call transcript into Claude Chat and begins refining an investment thesis before writing a single sentence.  Claude Chat asks whether the output is for an investment committee, clients, or internal research, then tailors the analysis accordingly. → A finance associate updates a DCF model inside Microsoft 365.  Claude incorporates new company guidance, adjusts assumptions such as the cost of debt, recalculates valuation inputs, and turns the results into a presentation without requiring manual rework. → A procurement team uploads multiple vendor contracts and receives a consolidated comparison of pricing, terms, and service-level agreements in minutes rather than days using Claude Cowork. → A quantitative analyst uses Claude Code to build and test pricing models, instantly seeing the impact of different discount structures on margins. → A wealth management platform uses the Claude API to generate personalized portfolio commentary for thousands of clients at scale. → A compliance team deploys managed agents that repeatedly review valuations and documentation with built-in guardrails, permissions, and audit trails. Research cycles become shorter.  Reviews happen faster.  Reporting takes less effort.  Teams spend less time moving information between systems and more time making decisions. In your opinion, which of these six use cases would save your team the most hours this quarter? In the next edition of the Atlas Newsletter, we\'ll provide a complete guide on how to install and use Claude\'s Finance plugins. Stay tuned. Distribution in the AI era: startups who will win the race  This is for companies wanting to scale their distribution and go to market quicker, even if they’re launching from zero. Steve Nouri is the founder of GenAI Works, the largest AI community on LinkedIn with 14M+ followers. He advises Fortune 100 companies on AI adoption and content distribution. Australia\'s ICT Professional of the Year. He’ll share: ✅ The channels and winning content patterns still working in 2026 ✅ Examples from companies he has advised ✅ A distribution playbook PDF you can apply within a week Register now. GTM Playbook PDF sent to all attendees. 📅 Thu, Jun 11 ⏰ 1 pm EDT | 10am PST Why is China forcing its biggest tech companies to stop buying Nvidia’s AI chips? Beijing didn\'t wait for Nvidia to run out of options. It closed the door itself. China\'s Cyberspace Administration reportedly ordered ByteDance, Alibaba, and other major technology companies to stop purchasing Nvidia\'s RTX Pro 6000D.  The chip was created specifically for China after U.S. export restrictions prevented Nvidia from selling its most advanced AI processors in the country. Companies that had already placed large orders were instructed to halt testing and stop supplier work immediately. This follows earlier restrictions on Nvidia\'s H20 chip. Together, the two decisions effectively shut down Nvidia\'s remaining large-volume AI chip business in China. Nvidia shares fell about 3% following the news. The decision was not simply a ban. It was a message. Chinese regulators spent months evaluating domestic alternatives from companies such as Huawei and Cambricon.  Their conclusion was that local chips had reached performance levels comparable to, or in some cases beyond, the Nvidia products still available to Chinese customers. Once that threshold was crossed, procurement policy followed. The impact reaches far beyond Nvidia. Governments around the world are increasingly asking the same question: can critical technology be built at home rather than imported? China has now answered that question with purchasing power. Hundreds of millions of dollars in future AI infrastructure spending could be redirected toward domestic suppliers. Chinese chipmakers are already targeting major increases in AI processor production next year. And technology self-sufficiency is becoming a procurement policy. As more countries prioritize domestic technology, is your business prepared for the impact on the platforms, suppliers, and ecosystems it depends on? How Gemini Embedding 2 is reducing the Cost and Complexity of Enterprise AI? If your enterprise is struggling with rising AI costs, Gemini Embedding 2 may offer a solution. Most organizations store valuable knowledge across documents, meetings, customer calls, videos, images, and technical content.  Most AI systems can only search a small part of that information effectively.  As a result, organizations often rely on multiple systems and retrieval pipelines, increasing both cost and complexity.  Google DeepMind\'s Gemini Embedding 2 is designed to change that. It maps all content types into a single searchable space. But why does this mapping matter? Because retrieval is the foundation of enterprise AI, if an AI assistant cannot find the right information, it cannot generate the right answer.  Due to that, your business will be impacted. So by implementing this model, information that was difficult and expensive to access can now become available through a single search experience. This can:  improve employee productivity reduce the cost of managing enterprise knowledge  increase the value organizations get from the data they already own The approach is not without challenges.  A single retrieval layer can reduce complexity and cost, but it can also make it harder to trace errors and explain AI outputs.  For regulated industries, maintaining transparency and auditability will remain essential. What could your business achieve if all of its knowledge were searchable in one place? Everything else you shouldn’t miss CodeRabbit built an entire agent orchestration system on Claude: The code review platform describes how it architected multi-agent coordination using Claude as the reasoning backbone. SpaceX is nearly done writing its own AI training stack in C: The in-house system maps directly to 220,000 GB300s with 800G NICs and uses heavy pipeline parallelism. Elon Musk says the speed improvement over JAX for large training runs could exceed an order of magnitude. Arm\'s AI security tool caught 98% of known vulnerabilities: Traditional static analysis tools caught 6%. Metis runs on GPT-5.5-Cyber via OpenAI Daybreak across 352 firmware and driver test cases. Harvard Business School mapped how AI use at work has shifted in 2026: The research covers creativity, productivity and decision-making as organizations move from basic adoption toward agentic systems handling end-to-end tasks. Learn more about AI from the experts building it 📸 Follow us on Instagram for fast, visual AI updates in 30 seconds.  🐝 Subscribe to our Generative AI daily newsletter — trusted by 120 000+ subscribers — to stay ahead of the latest AI news across tech, education, and business.  📺 Watch us on YouTube to hear insights directly from leading AI voices, builders, and innovators. 🐦 Follow us on X for breaking AI news and real-time industry updates. 🧠 Learn how to build your next AI application with practical resources and expert guidance. 🚀 Explore investment opportunities in the future of AI and join our community-backed growth journey. PS: Want to share your AI tool or company news with our 14M+ community? Get in touch.\nKeep reading on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/claude-just-changed-economics-enterprise-ai-genai-works-1xvhe?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BNje0ToPWTBukh0ARwdk%2BTQ%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=2by5L5KGM9IIg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_-null-icq8ji~mpr4a9hp~g3-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mpr4a9hp-g3\n  \n      \n\n----------------------------------------\n\nThis email was intended for Yashica Lohar (Flipkart GWC 7.0 Scholar | CSE ’28 @ IIIT Jabalpur | 2 ⭐ @Codechef)\nLearn why we included this: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/4788?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BNje0ToPWTBukh0ARwdk%2BTQ%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=2by5L5KGM9IIg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mpr4a9hp~g3-null-null&ei