ned to enhance your communication and productivity.\n\nWith the desktop app, you can:\n* Capture and annotate screenshots for clearer feedback.\n* Record your screen to create informative videos.\n* Create GIFs to share quick visual snippets.\n* Share files instantly with a link - no bulky attachments.\n\nThese tools allow you to share your work, ideas and feedback visually, making collaboration with your team effortless and more effective.\n\nDownload Jumpshare https://open.jumpshare.com/f/a/pB6CPtUUWv0rqy0nTg0REQ~~/AABzJxA~/ogQXfPFg9KeQSLrzpYxCzolWp7OJeKewMwBe8nLImRyXkWI29TGT7WOVmvcOb5UscZqT38ZN2vquZxYUvDJ_sRGnQ9cvuO310pv_4VsQWEVWXYeSehaWJf5IgtRslQ06\nIf you have any questions or need assistance, feel free to reach out. We\'re here to help you get the most out of Jumpshare!\n\nBest regards,\nThe Jumpshare Team\n\nJumpshare, Inc. (c) 2026','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('ad4656ea-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear Jumpshare,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"Just one more step to complete your setup\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('ad4f300b-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Atlas\n\nBy GenAI Works\n\n\nBy GenAI Works\n\n    \n    \n    Read this article on LinkedIn to join the conversation\nRead on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/how-ai-moving-from-assistants-autonomous-systems-genai-works-agrof?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BMYHQvlupQKCRwEgcS04%2B5A%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=0iHwsuitqvMYg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_-null-icq8ji~mpvl04ud~g3-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mpvl04ud-g3\n  \nWelcome back! This week, AI took another step away from chatbots and closer to autonomous execution. Claude gains financial research capabilities that can turn a simple prompt into an analyst-style report. Anthropic brings real-time security review directly into the coding process, helping developers catch vulnerabilities before code reaches production. Google introduces an autonomous security platform that moves vulnerabilities from discovery to remediation with minimal human intervention. Meanwhile, LlamaIndex eliminates one of the biggest bottlenecks in AI pipelines by rebuilding its document parser from the ground up and achieving dramatic performance gains. Different stories, one clear trend: AI is moving from assisting work to performing work.  In today\'s Generative AI Newsletter: Claude Finance Plugins: How to turn Claude into a financial research assistant in under 5 minutes? Claude Code Security Plugin: How Anthropic gave every developer a free security reviewer inside their coding environment? LiteParse v2.0: Why is document parsing the hidden bottleneck in most AI agent stacks? And how does a Rust rewrite change that? Google AI Threat Defense: How Google automated the full security lifecycle from vulnerability discovery to production patch? PS: Want to share your AI tool or company news with our 13M+ community? Get in touch. How to install Claude’s Finance plugins? Anthropic\'s Finance plugins turn Claude into a financial research assistant. Instead of manually reading earnings transcripts, filings, and market reports, you can simply ask Claude in plain English. Need a morning brief on a stock? Type: /morning-note on Apple Within seconds, Claude generates a structured summary based on recent filings, earnings information, and publicly available data. Want to explore a sector? Use the Market Research and Equity Research plugins to screen companies, identify trends, and generate investment ideas. The four plugins most retail investors need are: Financial Analysis: Valuations, financial modelling, and comparable company analysis. Equity Research: Stock screens, earnings updates, and company coverage. Earnings Reviewer: Morning notes and earnings summaries for companies you follow. Market Researcher: Sector overviews and idea generation. For most investors, the four plugins above are enough to get started. Getting started takes only a few minutes. The plugins live inside Claude\'s Cowork environment, which is available through the desktop application. To install them: 1️⃣ Open Claude Desktop and switch to Cowork. 2️⃣ Go to Customize → Browse Plugins → Personal. 3️⃣ Add a marketplace from GitHub. 4️⃣ Paste the Finance Marketplace repository URL: https://github.com/anthropics/financial-services-plugins 5️⃣ Synchronize and install the plugins you want. Once you finish, run: /morning-note on Apple and share your results in the comments. Oracle became a strategic partner with GenAI Works. The company is now raising its next round. Oracle is now a strategic partner of GenAI Works. A working partnership across content, events, and community. Oracle joins a client and partner ecosystem that includes Google, IBM, Nvidia, ElevenLabs, Bright Data. 300+ enterprise and startup clients in total. The partnership comes as GenAI Works continues its growth trajectory, increasing revenue 2.5× over the past year while expanding its global community and AI ecosystem. Building the infrastructure that helps organizations adopt AI at scale requires partners who understand both technology and execution. Oracle does. We\'re excited about what comes next. If you\'d like to be part of the next chapter of GenAI Works and help shape the future of AI education and adoption, let\'s collaborate. Join the round 𝘐𝘯 𝘮𝘢𝘬𝘪𝘯𝘨 𝘢𝘯 𝘪𝘯𝘷𝘦𝘴𝘵𝘮𝘦𝘯𝘵 𝘥𝘦𝘤𝘪𝘴𝘪𝘰𝘯, 𝘪𝘯𝘷𝘦𝘴𝘵𝘰𝘳𝘴 𝘮𝘶𝘴𝘵 𝘳𝘦𝘭𝘺 𝘰𝘯 𝘵𝘩𝘦𝘪𝘳 𝘰𝘸𝘯 𝘦𝘹𝘢𝘮𝘪𝘯𝘢𝘵𝘪𝘰𝘯 𝘰𝘧 𝘵𝘩𝘦 𝘪𝘴𝘴𝘶𝘦𝘳 𝘢𝘯𝘥 𝘵𝘩𝘦 𝘵𝘦𝘳𝘮𝘴 𝘰𝘧 𝘵𝘩𝘦 𝘰𝘧𝘧𝘦𝘳𝘪𝘯𝘨, 𝘪𝘯𝘤𝘭𝘶𝘥𝘪𝘯𝘨 𝘵𝘩𝘦 𝘮𝘦𝘳𝘪𝘵𝘴 𝘢𝘯𝘥 𝘳𝘪𝘴𝘬𝘴 𝘪𝘯𝘷𝘰𝘭𝘷𝘦𝘥. 𝘎𝘦𝘯𝘢𝘪 𝘞𝘰𝘳𝘬𝘴, 𝘐𝘯𝘤. 𝘩𝘢𝘴 𝘧𝘪𝘭𝘦𝘥 𝘢 𝘍𝘰𝘳𝘮 𝘊 𝘸𝘪𝘵𝘩 𝘵𝘩𝘦 𝘚𝘦𝘤𝘶𝘳𝘪𝘵𝘪𝘦𝘴 𝘢𝘯𝘥 𝘌𝘹𝘤𝘩𝘢𝘯𝘨𝘦 𝘊𝘰𝘮𝘮𝘪𝘴𝘴𝘪𝘰𝘯 𝘪𝘯 𝘤𝘰𝘯𝘯𝘦𝘤𝘵𝘪𝘰𝘯 𝘸𝘪𝘵𝘩 𝘪𝘵𝘴 𝘰𝘧𝘧𝘦𝘳𝘪𝘯𝘨, 𝘢 𝘤𝘰𝘱𝘺 𝘰𝘧 𝘸𝘩𝘪𝘤𝘩 𝘮𝘢𝘺 𝘣𝘦 𝘰𝘣𝘵𝘢𝘪𝘯𝘦𝘥 𝘩𝘦𝘳𝘦 How to install Anthropic\'s free security plugin for Claude Code? Most security bugs are found too late. During code reviews. During penetration tests. Or even worse... after deployment. Anthropic\'s new security plugin changes that. It gave every developer a free security reviewer inside Claude Code. It runs directly inside Claude Code and checks your code while you\'re writing it. What exactly does this plugin do? The plugin can spot: Hardcoded API keys Command injection risks Unsafe function calls Vulnerable libraries And when it finds an issue, it immediately suggests a fix. What makes this interesting is the timing. Finding a secret key before a commit is very different from finding it after it has been pushed to GitHub. The earlier you catch a problem, the cheaper it is to fix. For development teams, it means security becomes part of the coding process instead of a separate step. For solo developers, it\'s like having a security expert reviewing your work in real time. Would you trust an AI security reviewer to check your code before every commit? Share your thoughts. Subscribe here to get a complete guide of how the plugin works inside Claude Code. Don’t miss it. Why is document parsing still the bottleneck in your AI agent stack? If your team is struggling with slow document parsing, you might want to take a look at LiteParse v2.0 from LlamaIndex. The entire library was rebuilt in Rust. Now it runs also natively across Python, Node, Rust and WASM, including in the browser and on edge runtimes.  One codebase, every environment. The performance improvements are significant: → 5x - 100x faster on small documents compared to v1 → Around 3x faster on large documents → A 457-page, 100MB PDF can be parsed in under a second The speedup comes from eliminating architectural overhead.  The previous version relied on spinning up a Node process for each parse.  The new Rust implementation removes that dependency and optimizes every layer of the pipeline.  Other features: ✓ Supports 50+ document formats ✓ No LLM dependency required ✓ Preserves document structure and layout instead of flattening everything into plain text ✓ Runs fully client-side through WASM for privacy-sensitive workloads ✓ Open source and free For agent builders, the integration is straightforward: # Python: pip install liteparse # Node: npm i @llamaindex/liteparse # Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode: npx skills add run-llama/llamaparse-agent-skills --skill liteparse As AI models continue to get faster, document ingestion is increasingly becoming the hidden bottleneck in agent pipelines.  Have you measured the document parsing latency in your AI stack recently?  How can Google AI Threat Defense protect your assets?  Attackers are now using AI too. Finding weaknesses and launching attacks used to take days or weeks. Today, it can happen in hours. Google\'s response is to automate the entire security lifecycle. The Google AI Threat Defense platform combines: Wiz for attack surface visibility and risk prioritization Gemini for code analysis and vulnerability discovery CodeMender for automated remediation Mandiant for threat intelligence Together, they create a continuous security loop. But how do these 4 components work together? Discover: Wiz continuously maps applications, APIs, identities, and cloud environments. It actively tests whether the identified vulnerabilities can actually be exploited. Prioritize: Gemini scans for weaknesses. Wiz adds business context, exploitability, and reachability data. The result? Security teams focus on risks that matter instead of drowning in alerts. Remediate: This is where things get interesting. Google\'s new CodeMender agent generates fixes for the identified vulnerabilities Update dependencies. Test patches. Prepare them for deployment. Monitor: Security agents continuously watch production environments, hunt for threats, and verify system integrity. How long does it currently take your organization to move from vulnerability discovery to production remediation? Everything else you shouldn’t miss: Microsoft is building a super app: The company is working on a single application that combines Copilot chat, coding tools and other AI capabilities into one unified experience. Nvidia\'s RTX Spark brings 1 petaflop of AI to your laptop: The new superchip is designed for personal AI agents running locally on Windows devices, with all-day battery life. OpenAI is hiring for robotics: Sam Altman posted that the company envisions everyone owning a personal robot capable of handling any task they need. OpenAI launched Rosalind Biodefense: The platform gives the US government and vetted partners access to OpenAI\'s biology AI for pandemic preparedness and outbreak response. Learn more about AI from the experts building it 📸 Follow us on Instagram for fast, visual AI updates in 30 seconds.  🐝 Subscribe to our Generative AI daily newsletter — trusted by 120 000+ subscribers — to stay ahead of the latest AI news across tech, education, and business.  📺 Watch us on YouTube to hear insights directly from leading AI voices, builders, and innovators. 🐦 Follow us on X for breaking AI news and real-time industry updates. 🧠 Learn how to build your next AI application with practical resources and expert guidance. 🚀 Explore investment opportunities in the future of AI and join our community-backed growth journey. PS: Want to share your AI tool or company news with our 14M+ community? Get in touch.\nKeep reading on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/how-ai-moving-from-assistants-autonomous-systems-genai-works-agrof?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BMYHQvlupQKCRwEgcS04%2B5A%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=0iHwsuitqvMYg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_