it comes to well-being in the workplace, our behaviors are contagious. Your choices influence others, even if they don’t realize it. Each of us should consider how to maintain our energy and well-being, creating a supportive network among colleagues.\nRole modeling for others\n- Set expectations and boundaries - and communicate them\n	- Share what is going on, and ask for support\n	- Develop team norms\n	- Celebrate one another\nYour Personal Progress Update for Core Skills Level Courses\n- Your Adaptability and Resilience digital lesson status is: Not Started\n	- Your Problem Solving digital lesson status is: Not Started\n	- Your Communicating for Impact digital lesson status is: Not Started\n	- Your Relationships & Wellbeing digital lesson status is: Not Started\n	- Your My Digital Toolkit: Digital and AI Essentials digital lesson status is: Not Started\nDid you sign up for the Lead Forward webinar and submit the attendance verification form afterward?\nPlease register for the Lead Forward: Mindsets for Growth webinar if you haven\'t already. Note that attendance at Lead Forward is mandatory and a prerequisite for graduation.\n\nAfter attending, make sure to submit the attendance verification form to confirm your participation. If you submitted the form before the webinar, please re-submit it after attending.\nMcKinsey Accelerate Mobile App URL: https://academy.mckinseyaccelerate.com/ <https://links.mckinsey.com/NDczLVpZRS01MjIAAAGiJo_T4KP6SEJdqKafC2u_wlDfwnFJ7SlPXFtAxqRGYrtilEEB3enGcz61Jvg6ubs1NfgZyVY=>\nKind regards,\n The McKinsey.org Forward Team\nNeed Help? \n\n You are receiving this email from an account we use for outbound emails only. We have created these resources to help you have a smooth journey:\nFind the answer in our Forward Solution Hub <https://links.mckinsey.com/NDczLVpZRS01MjIAAAGiJo_T4H1kRk0Y_UVhGCvwhkb8g25JZq6PBz0fcByPdE6FiI-LCdapy2A--vgpOVJCsjdyl9M=>\nUse our Forward Solution Hub to find answers to the frequently asked questions.\n\n© McKinsey & Company, Inc. \n 175 Greenwich Street \n New York, NY 10007 \n United States\n\nThis email contains operational information regarding your progress in McKinsey’s Forward Program. By opening our emails or clicking on links you agree to our use of cookies and web tracking technology. For more information on how we use and protect your information, please review our privacy policy <https://www.mckinsey.com/privacy-policy>. If you prefer not to receive future email communications from us, please click here <https://links.mckinsey.com/NDczLVpZRS01MjIAAAGiJo_T4Eb1RbQNUewPTCn2oV0E7g0QAyGs-4SebHe01-ujHeCUdAcFvNev8ODp4N-G4HPyTPA=> to unsubscribe from all McKinsey communications. Please note, however, that these emails are transactional in nature and are sent while you remain a participant in the program. Unsubscribing from general commercial communications related to McKinsey’s research, insights, services or events will not automatically exclude you from receiving these operational messages, unless you explicitly request otherwise.\n\nThis email was sent to loharyashica@gmail.com. If you no longer wish to receive these emails you may unsubscribe here: https://pages.mckinsey.com/Unsubscribed.html?mkt_unsubscribe=1&mkt_tok=NDczLVpZRS01MjIAAAGiJo_T4BXCmn0ZN65nB6OGo7YuAs4w0lOTCd7PmG2bLUQgOwFyVZzvVHwKUQJ55V74Zv8V8JJpw0o21SK1ZzQc6iO5rdHjXhRi1NJGOtYa34mgXS-ZTA.\n','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('ad5fbc8d-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear Forward Learners,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"4 Weeks Left: Stay on Track!\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('ad68fff7-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Podcasting Made Simple\n\nBy Alex Sanfilippo\n\n\nBy Alex Sanfilippo\n\n    \n    \n    Read this article on LinkedIn to join the conversation\nRead on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/how-podcasting-can-build-trust-engagement-distracted-world-alex-ryffe?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BjautnCybQMO%2FiqfSKCVTAQ%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=1UrSQsWxLQNYg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_-null-icq8ji~mpwnunej~66-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mpwnunej-66\n  \nWe live in a world that’s more distracted than ever before. It seems impossible to cut through all the noise. But thankfully, there’s something you can do to get noticed! In this episode, Mehmet Gonullu explains how you can use podcasting to establish real trust by choosing depth and transparency over hype in your content. Get ready to stop seeking attention and start building trust that lasts! 🎧 Watch or Listen to This Episode of Podcasting Made Simple: https://PodMatch.com/Episodes (Then Search \"386\") 📝 Big Ideas From This Episode: 1. Trust is the real currency In a loud, fast feed, people tune out hype. A steady voice, honest questions, and real listening build trust that lasts longer than any post. 2. Trade reach for resonance Stop trying to impress everyone. Speak to the right people. When they hear how you think over time, they feel aligned and they lean in. 3. Lead with genuine curiosity Curiosity is hard to fake. Ask what you actually want to know, follow the thread, and let the guest’s answer shape the next question. 4. Create a safe place for real stories Great moments happen when guests feel safe. Set the tone, remove pressure, and make it clear this is a conversation, not a performance review. 5. Podcasting rewards depth Short platforms reward quick hits. Podcasting rewards depth, nuance, and context. Depth is where trust forms, especially in B2B and expertise. Attend Podcasting Made Simple Live For Free by visiting https://PodMatch.com/event and use code PMLIVE! 6. Presence beats performance Forget polished. Be present. Listeners notice your follow ups, your pauses, and what you choose not to say. That is where credibility shows up. 7. Ask the questions others skip Be the person who asks what no one else asks, then shuts up and listens. The best insights live behind the first, easy answer. 8. Consistency builds reputation One episode is content. A consistent body of work is reputation. Integrity compounds when people hear the same values from you for months. 9. Guests should serve, not pitch Show up to help the listener, not to sell the listener. Share lessons, context, and mistakes. Trust grows when the audience feels respected. 10. Alignment opens doors When you build trust, you stop chasing opportunities. The right people reach out because they already know how you think and how you operate. 💡 Final Thought: Podcasting is a relationship engine in a distracted world. When hosts and guests choose curiosity, presence, and depth, trust forms naturally. Trust leads to real engagement because people feel safe, seen, and understood. Over time, those conversations turn into partnerships, referrals, and opportunities that no viral moment can replace. 💬 Did you listen to or watch this episode of Podcasting Made Simple? If yes, what was your biggest takeaway?\nKeep reading on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/how-podcasting-can-build-trust-engagement-distracted-world-alex-ryffe?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BjautnCybQMO%2FiqfSKCVTAQ%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=1UrSQsWxLQNYg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_-null-icq8ji~mpwnunej~66-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mpwnunej-66\n  \n      \n\n----------------------------------------\n\nThis email was intended for Yashica Lohar (Flipkart GWC 7.0 Scholar | CSE ’28 @ IIIT Jabalpur | 2 ⭐ @Codechef)\nLearn why we included this: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/4788?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BjautnCybQMO%2FiqfSKCVTAQ%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=1UrSQsWxLQNYg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mpwnunej~66-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mpwnunej-66\nYou are receiving LinkedIn notification emails. Others can see that you are a subscriber.\n\n\nUnsubscribe: https://www.linkedin.com/series-notifications/?action=unsubscribe&memberToken=ADoAAEIlwb4B7wSObgzu320aKxhPrfHhU2UtxwY&newsletterId=7069288237738942464&newsletterTitle=Podcasting Made Simple&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BjautnCybQMO%2FiqfSKCVTAQ%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=1UrSQsWxLQNYg1&ek=email_series_follow_newsletter_02&e=icq8ji-mpwnunej-66&eid=icq8ji-mpwnunej-66&m=unsubscribe&ts=footerGlimmer&li=0&t=plh    ·  Help: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/67?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BjautnCybQMO%2FiqfSKCVTAQ%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=1UrSQsWxLQNYg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-help-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-help-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mpwnunej~66-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mpwnunej-66\n\n© 2026 LinkedIn Corporation, 1zwnj000 West Maude Avenue, Sunnyvale, CA 94085.\nLinkedIn and the LinkedIn logo are registered trademarks of LinkedIn.','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('ad69a062-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear Podcasting Made Simple,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"How Podcasting Can Build Trust and Engagement in a Distracted World\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issu