1 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('ad7d9d46-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear Pinterest,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"All it takes is one good idea\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('ad84e338-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'LinkedIn 360 l By GaryVee\n\nBy Gary Vaynerchuk\n\n\nBy Gary Vaynerchuk\n\n    \n    \n    Read this article on LinkedIn to join the conversation\nRead on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/instagram-stories-dilemma-gary-vaynerchuk-m0p7e?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BIhs033jSQkSkb15G3zi2Fg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=0lEcnjKnMFOsg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_-null-icq8ji~mpwzo8tk~1j-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mpwzo8tk-1j\n  \nStop obsessing over your Instagram grid One of the biggest mistakes creators, influencers, and brands are making right now is confusing Instagram Stories with actually posting content. People are desperately trying to fit into an ideological framework that quantity hurts quality. Or it’s just a disguise that they don’t want to put in the work ethic to out-index the competitors battling for attention in their categories. This is basically the plight of every creator right now. Creators tend to get comfortable and cozy on one or two platforms. They’re not expanding to enough platforms. They’re not expanding handle strategy. They’re not posting enough on each platform…and Instagram Stories have become one of the easiest ways for people to convince themselves they’re doing more than they actually are. Stories Feel Productive. They Aren\'t the Same as Posting I hear it all the time. “Gary, I post four times a day.” Then I look, and they’re posting four Stories a day and one feed post every three days. Instagram has become most people’s personal website. They want their profile to tell a story. They want their grid to look a certain way, and they want people who visit their page to see videos with lots of views. They’re choosing optics over results. The irony is that a shocking percentage of content on Instagram is consumed in the feed. Think about it this way. Your entire town is ordering food through Uber Eats, Seamless, and Postmates. That’s how everybody eats…and you’re obsessed with how your restaurant looks from the street. That’s what many creators are doing with Instagram. They’re spending enormous energy curating the storefront while ignoring where the actual consumption is happening. Now let me be clear. Instagram Stories are not bad. They’re a great additive since they were introduced in 2016. In fact, for some people they’re an incredible format, but they are not a substitute for posting. You do not get the same reach potential in Stories that you do in feed content. Stories are a nice complement. Feed content is where awareness gets built. The bigger issue here is that people are looking for loopholes, and I’m tired of people being cute and saying they post four times a day when it’s really one feed post every two days and four Stories a day. The Game Is Attention Underneath that behavior is a much larger problem: not enough platforms, not enough handles, not enough content, and then those same people end up in my DMs asking why it isn’t working. Now, here’s the disclaimer. If you’re happy, if you’re content, if you’re getting exactly what you want from social media, then post once a year. Post once in a lifetime. Do whatever makes you happy. But if you’re emailing me, DMing me, or asking why your brand isn’t growing, why your audience isn’t growing, why your business isn’t growing, then we need to have a different conversation. You’re not making enough content. Stop Hiding. Start Publishing The cost of entry has gone up. The amount of content required to build awareness today is dramatically higher than it was five years ago. So much of winning social media is about hitting singles and doubles with the occasional grand slam and trying not to strike out. Most people are waiting for the grand slam, and they’re waiting for perfection. They’re waiting for the perfect post. They’re waiting for certainty. Meanwhile, the people winning are simply putting more balls in play. That’s what this article is really about. Instagram Stories aren’t the problem. The excuse is the problem. The Instagram Stories Dilemma is simply one symptom of a larger issue: too many creators are optimizing for comfort, optics, and curation when they should be optimizing for reach, awareness, and relevance. The answer isn’t complicated: post more, post on more platforms, stop hiding behind Stories, and start putting more content into the feed.\nKeep reading on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/instagram-stories-dilemma-gary-vaynerchuk-m0p7e?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BIhs033jSQkSkb15G3zi2Fg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=0lEcnjKnMFOsg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_-null-icq8ji~mpwzo8tk~1j-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mpwzo8tk-1j\n  \n      \n\n----------------------------------------\n\nThis email was intended for Yashica Lohar (Flipkart GWC 7.0 Scholar | CSE ’28 @ IIIT Jabalpur | 2 ⭐ @Codechef)\nLearn why we included this: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/4788?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BIhs033jSQkSkb15G3zi2Fg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=0lEcnjKnMFOsg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mpwzo8tk~1j-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mpwzo8tk-1j\nYou are receiving LinkedIn notification emails. Others can see that you are a subscriber.\n\n\nUnsubscribe: https://www.linkedin.com/series-notifications/?action=unsubscribe&memberToken=ADoAAEIlwb4B7wSObgzu320aKxhPrfHhU2UtxwY&newsletterId=6641420720876343296&newsletterTitle=LinkedIn 360 l By GaryVee&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BIhs033jSQkSkb15G3zi2Fg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=0lEcnjKnMFOsg1&ek=email_series_follow_newsletter_02&e=icq8ji-mpwzo8tk-1j&eid=icq8ji-mpwzo8tk-1j&m=unsubscribe&ts=footerGlimmer&li=0&t=plh    ·  Help: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/67?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BIhs033jSQkSkb15G3zi2Fg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=0lEcnjKnMFOsg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-help-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-help-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mpwzo8tk~1j-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mpwzo8tk-1j\n\n© 2026 LinkedIn Corporation, 1zwnj000 West Maude Avenue, Sunnyvale, CA 94085.\nLinkedIn and the LinkedIn logo are registered trademarks of LinkedIn.','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('ad85a318-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear LinkedIn 360 l By GaryVee,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"The Instagram Stories Dilemma\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('ad967a39-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'----------------------------------------\n\nThis email was intended for Yashica Lohar (Flipkart GWC 7.0 Scholar | CSE ’28 @ IIIT Jabalpur | 2 ⭐ @Codechef)\nLearn why we included this: https://www