 read this, please download Whatnot, the live shopping app, if you haven\'t already, and bookmark this show or just come to it at 11 p.m. Eastern tonight. On tonight\'s show, we launch our new trading card drop, 2026 Topps Chrome VeeFriends. If you don\'t know about this collectible yet, check out these eBay auctions. Please come and watch me as I give away a $5,000 case of trading cards. I\'ll be giving away over 200 packs for free. Come and get yours. Learn about our incredible Harry Potter Marvel Disney-like universe but more importantly learn how I\'m using live shopping as a platform to build this brand. Something all of you can impose on your personal brand, your startup or your corporation. Can\'t wait to see you tonight. Pass this on to anyone who\'s curious about Pokemon cards, collectibles or live shopping.\nJoin the conversation\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/free-education-live-shopping-tonight-11pm-et-too-gary-vaynerchuk-eau1e?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3Bthgy8wGcTy2nbfxUNhvEPg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=0T-Lmt6-EjXYg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_-null-icq8ji~mq6mgby5~tk-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mq6mgby5-tk\n  \n      \n\n----------------------------------------\n\nThis email was intended for Yashica Lohar (Flipkart GWC 7.0 Scholar | CSE ’28 @ IIIT Jabalpur | 2 ⭐ @Codechef)\nLearn why we included this: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/4788?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3Bthgy8wGcTy2nbfxUNhvEPg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=0T-Lmt6-EjXYg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mq6mgby5~tk-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mq6mgby5-tk\nYou are receiving LinkedIn notification emails. Others can see that you are a subscriber.\n\n\nUnsubscribe: https://www.linkedin.com/series-notifications/?action=unsubscribe&memberToken=ADoAAEIlwb4B7wSObgzu320aKxhPrfHhU2UtxwY&newsletterId=6641420720876343296&newsletterTitle=LinkedIn 360 l By GaryVee&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3Bthgy8wGcTy2nbfxUNhvEPg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=0T-Lmt6-EjXYg1&ek=email_series_follow_newsletter_02&e=icq8ji-mq6mgby5-tk&eid=icq8ji-mq6mgby5-tk&m=unsubscribe&ts=footerGlimmer&li=0&t=plh    ·  Help: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/67?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3Bthgy8wGcTy2nbfxUNhvEPg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=0T-Lmt6-EjXYg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-help-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-help-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mq6mgby5~tk-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mq6mgby5-tk\n\n© 2026 LinkedIn Corporation, 1zwnj000 West Maude Avenue, Sunnyvale, CA 94085.\nLinkedIn and the LinkedIn logo are registered trademarks of LinkedIn.','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('af28b047-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear LinkedIn 360 l By GaryVee,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"Free Education on Live Shopping Tonight at 11pm ET + Free Collectibles, Too\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('af2ed27c-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Podcasting Made Simple\n\nBy Alex Sanfilippo\n\n\nBy Alex Sanfilippo\n\n    \n    \n    Read this article on LinkedIn to join the conversation\nRead on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/how-turn-your-podcast-guest-spots-paying-clients-alex-sanfilippo-dqude?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BImQCJnqIS5ae0CXFW8mGqw%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=3TgxQHCD1kXYg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_-null-icq8ji~mq6ohlap~80-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mq6ohlap-80\n  \nIf your podcast guest interviews feel great but lead to zero action, the issue isn’t your expertise; it’s clarity. Thankfully, that’s something that’s easy to adjust! In this episode, Lyndsay Phillips 🎙️ Guesting/ Repurposing Expert shares a simple way to communicate what you do so hosts and listeners understand, remember, and respond to your call to action. Get ready to speak to real problems, make your value obvious, and turn interviews into clients! 🎧 Watch or Listen to This Episode of Podcasting Made Simple: https://PodMatch.com/Episodes (Then Search \"387\") 📝 Big Ideas From This Episode: 1. Build the bridge Treat each guest spot like a bridge from the listener\'s pain to your offer. Guide them from struggle to solution and a clear next step. 2. Give a conversation compass Send the host a conversation compass: 5 to 8 questions that steer toward your expertise so the interview stays focused and your message lands. 3. Lay message pavers Build message pavers before you record. Write tight talking points so you sound clear, concise, and confident while still keeping it conversational. 4. Start with their pain Hook people by naming the pain in their words: what they feel, fear, and think. When they self identify fast, they keep listening for the fix. 5. Reframe the real problem After empathy, reframe the real problem from your perspective and share the shift. This positions your approach as the answer, not just more tips. Attend Podcasting Made Simple Live For Free by visiting https://PodMatch.com/event and use code PMLIVE! 6. Show the full transformation Share the full transformation, not a single tactic. Give context like pillars or phases so listeners see the depth of what you do and want more. 7. Seed your offers naturally Seed your programs naturally by describing how you help and what results look like. Paint a picture so curiosity rises without sounding salesy. 8. Use story sound bites Use story sound bites: short client moments with stakes, a turning point, and a result. They create emotion, credibility, and instant clarity. 9. Name your framework Differentiate by naming your method or framework. A clear system signals a proven process, raises perceived value, and helps you stand out quickly. 10. Practice then speak naturally Prepare in writing, then speak like a human. Stay organic while avoiding winging it so your answers become sharp, calm, memorable, and easy to act on. 💡 Final Thought: Guest spots convert when your message is clear, not when you try to say everything. Connect the listener\'s pain to a real process and back it with stories people remember. Treat the interview as relationship building with the host and the audience. Over time, those conversations create clients, referrals, and partnerships because trust came first. 💬 Did you listen to or watch this episode of Podcasting Made Simple? If yes, what was your biggest takeaway?\nKeep reading on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/how-turn-your-podcast-guest-spots-paying-clients-alex-sanfilippo-dqude?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BImQCJnqIS5ae0CXFW8mGqw%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=3TgxQHCD1kXYg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_-null-icq8ji~mq6ohlap~80-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mq6ohlap-80\n  \n      \n\n----------------------------------------\n\nThis email was intended for Yashica Lohar (Flipkart GWC 7.0 Scholar | CSE ’28 @ IIIT Jabalpur | 2 ⭐ @Codechef)\nLearn why we included this: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/4788?lang=en