ter_02%3BYB5B3WOSR%2BK6bEtQuVtfuA%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=2adbRxYhUzYcg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_-null-icq8ji~mq6w5gdt~ow-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mq6w5gdt-ow\n  \nAs the World Cup approaches, serious international debates are heating up. Like whether we should be calling it soccer or football. And if it\'s played on a field or a pitch. But something we can all agree on is that \"the beautiful game\" is most beautiful when all 11 players operate as a single team. Everyone gets better when each player knows their role, trusts their teammates, and can adapt in real time.  Hmm, that kind of sounds like the key to a well-designed human-agent workforce. That\'s the vision, at least. At most companies, true human-AI collaboration is still a work in progress. The businesses that are succeeding with AI aren\'t just relying on technology. They\'ve figured out how to train and empower employees to use that technology better. Here\'s what that looks like in the field. (Or pitch.) Why employees are giving AI a yellow card What do soccer, dipping french fries in mayo, and workplace AI have in common? Americans have been slower to embrace them vs. their global counterparts. The mayo hesitation is obvious. So is the AI-resistance: American employees still lack AI training, and are slow to trust AI and its outputs. That could be seen as a challenge for U.S. companies — or a checklist of what needs to change.  The right game plan has been shown to turn 76% of employees into AI advocates. It starts with leadership providing role-specific tools, proper onboarding, and AI that\'s baked into the platforms employees already use. Get everyone running the same play The average business uses 12 agents — a number that\'s expected to grow 67% in the next two years. But, like a soccer team where the defense, offense, and goalie have never practiced together, nearly half of those agents are still disconnected from the systems and people around them. That could lead to confusion, distrust, and incorrect responses — the AI equivalent of kicking a goal into your own net. This practical framework makes sure that everyone\'s running the same play: Human task + agent task + trust guardrails. Get the positions right and the whole team will play better. That\'s the ticket A ticket to the World Cup is one of the priciest seats in sports, yet millions of fans are willing to pay for one. That\'s the kind of customer loyalty companies dream of. Many are trying to make it a reality by using agentic AI. While their agents close out service tickets, employees are focusing on building stronger relationships. But much like the technology they\'ve adopted, the skills that service organizations need are evolving. These 3 non-negotiables for service team leadership will help your employees use AI to turn every customer into a diehard fan. This newsletter was curated by Benny Spiewak, Senior Marketing Lead at Salesforce.\nKeep reading on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/how-help-employees-reach-gooooooals-salesforce-trowc?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BYB5B3WOSR%2BK6bEtQuVtfuA%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=2adbRxYhUzYcg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_-null-icq8ji~mq6w5gdt~ow-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mq6w5gdt-ow\n  \n      \n\n----------------------------------------\n\nThis email was intended for Yashica Lohar (Flipkart GWC 7.0 Scholar | CSE ’28 @ IIIT Jabalpur | 2 ⭐ @Codechef)\nLearn why we included this: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/4788?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BYB5B3WOSR%2BK6bEtQuVtfuA%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=2adbRxYhUzYcg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mq6w5gdt~ow-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mq6w5gdt-ow\nYou are receiving LinkedIn notification emails. Others can see that you are a subscriber.\n\n\nUnsubscribe: https://www.linkedin.com/series-notifications/?action=unsubscribe&memberToken=ADoAAEIlwb4B7wSObgzu320aKxhPrfHhU2UtxwY&newsletterId=7079504890934263808&newsletterTitle=Do More With AI&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BYB5B3WOSR%2BK6bEtQuVtfuA%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=2adbRxYhUzYcg1&ek=email_series_follow_newsletter_02&e=icq8ji-mq6w5gdt-ow&eid=icq8ji-mq6w5gdt-ow&m=unsubscribe&ts=footerGlimmer&li=0&t=plh    ·  Help: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/67?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BYB5B3WOSR%2BK6bEtQuVtfuA%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=2adbRxYhUzYcg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-help-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-help-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mq6w5gdt~ow-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mq6w5gdt-ow\n\n© 2026 LinkedIn Corporation, 1zwnj000 West Maude Avenue, Sunnyvale, CA 94085.\nLinkedIn and the LinkedIn logo are registered trademarks of LinkedIn.','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('af56f78e-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear Do More With AI,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"How To Help Employees Reach Their Gooooooals\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('af5fddb1-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'LinkedIn 360 l By GaryVee\n\nBy Gary Vaynerchuk\n\n\nBy Gary Vaynerchuk\n\n    \n    \n    Read this article on LinkedIn to join the conversation\nRead on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/9-things-you-need-know-wednesdays-veefriends-topps-gary-vaynerchuk-azy2e?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BE%2FTgeR76TZGZhsOKJwAkzg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=2uTIjMcfuXYsg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_-null-icq8ji~mq7aq3sf~vq-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mq7aq3sf-vq\n  \nI am literally building the next Pokemon in peoples faces. If you don’t know what VeeFriends is, it’s my Pokémon, Marvel, Disney, Harry Potter universe of 250+ characters trying to build positivity, practicality, and accountability to the world. On Wednesday June 10th, the brand new Topps Chrome VeeFriends set releases globally. If you haven’t dove into the universe of comic books, collectibles, cartoons, and so much more over the last 5 years – this is the set to start with and here is everything you need to know. 9 Things You Need to Know About This Wednesday’s VeeFriends-Topps Chrome Launch 1. On Wednesday at 1 PM EST, there will be a raffle for everyone to enter to try and win VeeFriends Chrome. It’s a very hot product in our world and the card hobby, so not everyone will win - but this is the chance to get Hobby, Mega, and Blaster Boxes at retail price. Here’s a breakdown of what I mean by those 3 box styles.  2. Select retailers across the country - Target, GameStop, and select Dick’s Sporting Goods - will have @VeeFriendsCardsTopps Chrome 2026 Blaster and Mega boxes at retail price, which are currently half the price of secondary eBay sales (ask if your local GameStop carries Hobby boxes). Hobby shops will also carry the product, just not always at retail price. If you miss out, there’s always people listing boxes on eBay. 3. We made a global store locator to help you all find 2026 VeeFriends Topps Chrome boxes across all major retail and hobby shop locations. Plug in your zip and see what’s nearby! On Wednesday, June 10th, Topps will host a public EQL drop at 11AM ET globally. Head to topps.com or your regional Topps website to enter. This drop is first-come, first-served, so be ready before the queue opens. 4. The full 2026 Topps Chrome VeeFriends set features 200 total characters, including 149 First Chrome appearances and 51 returning favorites. All characters, for example Gratitude Gorilla and Empathy Elephant, have huge collectors looking to track down cards from this year’s set. 5. Mr. Beast is getting his first ever signed trading card! It’s part of a set in this called “Content Condor’s Favorite Content Creators” and also includes creators like Livvy Dunne, Mel Robbins, and Kam Patterson getting their first chrome cards and autographs. The SuperFractor 1/1 MrBeast autograph is going to be a HUGE card for whoever pulls it! 6. You can stay in the loop and get all the latest details HERE 7. There’s an incredible tool for people wanting to learn and see more of the cards from a wonderful community member @Annebagg - where you can scroll through all the set’s characters and cards! 8. There’s a huge and very rare insert set called ERUPT! For those who know sports cards, you may know the popular Kaboom! set. The VeeFriends ERUPT! Insert is created by the same original artist, based in Budapest, Hungary. 9. THE #1 card to find comes from that set - the Superfractor 1/1 ERUPT Very, Very, Very, Very, Lucky Black Cat has a bounty from a top collector for $100,000… that can be pulled potentially from an $8 blaster pack. On Chrome Day - June 10th - I’m going all out. I’ll be making a marathon of livestream appearances throughout the day, so no matter when you’re watching, there’s a good chance I am live somewhere celebrating the global release of 2026 Topps Chrome VeeFriends with the community. Check the full schedule below and make sure you’re following along so you don’t miss a moment: 8:30 AM – 8:45 AM | Welcome Stranger Collectibles 9:00 AM – 9:15 AM | North Of 7 9:30 AM – 9:45 AM | Mama Breaks 9:45 AM – 10:00 AM | We The Hobby 10:00 AM – 10:15 AM | VIP Rips 10:15 AM – 10:30 AM |1of1cardshop 10:30 AM – 10:45 AM | BlackGold 11:00 AM – 11:15 AM | Swish Breaks 11:30 AM – 11:45 AM | Deep Fried Cards 12:00 PM – 12:15 PM | Gulf Coast / East West Wax 12:15 PM – 12:30 PM | Neighborhood Card Shop 12:30 PM – 12:45 PM | 528 Collectibles 1:00 PM – 1:15 PM | FreshWax 1:30 PM – 1:45 PM |Midwest 2:00 PM – 2:15 PM | Mintink 2:30 PM – 2:45 PM | We The Hobby Main 3:00 PM – 3:15 PM | Replay Sports Cards 3:30 PM – 3:45 PM | Pullwax 4:00 PM – 4:15 PM | Suncoast 4:30 PM – 5:00 PM | VeeFriends IRL — Gary Live @ Industrious 5:30 PM – 5:45 PM | Mamba Cards 5:45 PM – 6:00 PM | Bargain Hunters Thrift Store 6:00 PM – 6:15 PM | Monster Card Shop 6:15 PM – 6:30 PM | Layton Sports Cards 6:30 PM – 6:45 PM | Steel City Collectibles 6:45 PM – 7:00 PM | We The Hobby — In-Store See you June 10th!\nKeep reading on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/9-things-you-need-know-wednesdays-veefriends-topps-gary-vaynerchuk-azy2e?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BE%2FTgeR76TZGZhsOKJwAkzg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=2uTIjMcfuXYsg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_-null-icq8ji~mq7aq3sf~vq-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mq7aq3sf-vq\n  \n      \n\n----------------------------------------\n\nThis email was intended for Yashica Lohar (Flipkart GWC 7.0 Scholar | CSE ’28 @ IIIT Jabalpur | 2 ⭐ @Codechef)\nLearn why we included this: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/4788?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BE%2FTgeR76TZGZhsOKJwAkzg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=2uTIjMcfuXYsg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-Securi