NoIjogIjE4ODU5NzI5NjYxNDk1MzA5NDl8MTJ8MTB8MTcxNTQwMDQyIn0%3D&al_pri=8&aoid=4DBwmLZE0xT&aoty=4&aty=4&cp=12&et=2&id=23f1846a10254157bdbcda45f9a6d1b7&uid=YfxxO1ZRus7\n\n-----\n\n-----\n\nTo control which emails we send you, visit: https://www.quora.com/qemail/tc?aoid&aoty=14&aty=4&cp=0&et=2&id=23f1846a10254157bdbcda45f9a6d1b7&uid=YfxxO1ZRus7\n\nTo unsubscribe from this type of email, visit: https://www.quora.com/email_optout/qemail_unsubscribe?email_track_id=23f1846a10254157bdbcda45f9a6d1b7&t=1781061442643729&token=a2a470a6ea0f88ca73725f9a9394182dc86d29ee9eca479739c6b818e6374d0914cc30e490c48b979d915a120831fcc990d9b6999dc0dff37b1d0c03c91fbe12&type=2&uid=1952091097','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('af69ce74-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear Quora Digest,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"What is it like to earn 60 LPA in India?\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('af709217-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Zoho Bulletin\n\nBy Zoho\n\n\nBy Zoho\n\n    \n    \n    Read this article on LinkedIn to join the conversation\nRead on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/what-take-india-build-world-class-ai-zoho-adccf?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BMpznujDsTsuJqBjxkmWbVg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=30BHZkN4jUYIg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-null-0-read_more_banner_cta_-null-icq8ji~mq7ltr5g~h8-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mq7ltr5g-h8\n  \nHello everyone! Welcome to your monthly round-up of everything happening at Zoho. Last month, we backed India\'s open commerce network, shipped a major WorkDrive update, and earned industry recognition for Zoho RPA. Read on to see what else we\'ve been up to 👇 A conversation on building world-class tech in India Our co-founder and chief scientist Sridhar Vembu sat down to discuss exactly that on NPCI\'s Innovators Playground podcast. He and Dilip Asbe, MD and CEO of National Payments Corporation Of India (NPCI), talk about building deep tech from India, why the path here looks different from the West, and how rural talent and affordable AI could shape what comes next. Betting on India\'s digital backbone 🇮🇳 We\'re thrilled to announce a strategic investment in ONDC to support the growth of open digital commerce in India. An open, interoperable network like ONDC levels the playing field for businesses that could never build their own infrastructure. It\'s another step toward India owning its digital foundations—and one we\'re happy to be backing. Highlights from ET CIO Annual Conclave Last month, at #ETCIOAC26, we joined enterprise leaders from across India for two days of conversations on the questions defining tech right now: real-world AI execution, cybersecurity, and enterprise modernization. We were left with plenty to think about. Thank you to everyone who stopped by to chat with us! Introducing WorkDrive 6.0! Think about how much of your work day disappears into doing nothing in particular. You\'re hunting for that one file, rewatching a recorded meeting to catch one detail, or re-explaining context that already exists somewhere else. We built Zoho WorkDrive6.0 to fix that. Your files can now answer questions, summarize themselves, and point you to what you need before you go looking—all under the kind of governance enterprise teams can\'t go without. 😎 Have a look and tell us what you think! A Leader in RPA 🏆 Zoho RPA was named a Leader in the Nucleus Research 2026 RPA Technology Value Matrix, recognized for the balance of usability and business value it brings to enterprise automation. We\'re so thrilled to see Zoho recognized among the industry leaders shaping the future of RPA. A huge thank you to our team, customers, and partners for helping us push it this far! 🙏 Security must be the foundation for any digital business, not an afterthought For #WorldPasswordDay this year, we commissioned a global study of 3,300+ IT and security leaders, in 9 regions, to find out what\'s really putting businesses at risk. And the key finding was alarming: 1 in 3 businesses confirmed a cyberattack in the past year. Beyond getting the basics right and making security and privacy the foundation of everything you build, what can you do? Read the full State of Workforce Password Security report to find out. What does inclusive tech actually feel like? This #NationalTechDay, we put that question to the people who\'d know best—members of our customer and partner network who are working closely on community impact. Here are a few responses that stayed with us. The Long Game is now on Substack! 📫 In the first issue, we dig in to what to do when you\'re burnt out as a founder, why teams underperform, and what happens to creativity when you take AI out of the equation. We\'d love for you to check it out and subscribe while you\'re at it. From the horse\'s mouth Our partner ecosystem has always been central to how we grow—and lately it\'s been shifting to a more capability-led approach, without losing sight of customer success. In this conversation with DQ Channels, Bishan Singh, director of our Global Partner Program, breaks down what that shift looks like as the enterprise world goes AI-native, across a network of 3,000+ Partners in 100 countries. Humans of Zoho Over thirteen years at Zoho, Anish Mathew has learned that growth isn\'t about having all the answers. Quite the opposite, actually: The lesson is to stay open to learning, treat failure as part of the process, and give things (and people) a second chance. Watch him reflect on all this and more 👇 That\'s all for this issue of the Zoho Bulletin 👋 For all product updates, be sure to subscribe to Zoho Buzz. If you have any feedback or ideas, simply drop a comment below! See you in the next one! 👋\nKeep reading on LinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/comm/pulse/what-take-india-build-world-class-ai-zoho-adccf?lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BMpznujDsTsuJqBjxkmWbVg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=30BHZkN4jUYIg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-newsletter_content_preview_text-0-readmore_button_-null-icq8ji~mq7ltr5g~h8-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mq7ltr5g-h8\n  \n      \n\n----------------------------------------\n\nThis email was intended for Yashica Lohar (Flipkart GWC 7.0 Scholar | CSE ’28 @ IIIT Jabalpur | 2 ⭐ @Codechef)\nLearn why we included this: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/4788?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BMpznujDsTsuJqBjxkmWbVg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=30BHZkN4jUYIg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-SecurityHelp-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mq7ltr5g~h8-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mq7ltr5g-h8\nYou are receiving LinkedIn notification emails. Others can see that you are a subscriber.\n\n\nUnsubscribe: https://www.linkedin.com/series-notifications/?action=unsubscribe&memberToken=ADoAAEIlwb4B7wSObgzu320aKxhPrfHhU2UtxwY&newsletterId=7041659773024428032&newsletterTitle=The Zoho Bulletin&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BMpznujDsTsuJqBjxkmWbVg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=30BHZkN4jUYIg1&ek=email_series_follow_newsletter_02&e=icq8ji-mq7ltr5g-h8&eid=icq8ji-mq7ltr5g-h8&m=unsubscribe&ts=footerGlimmer&li=0&t=plh    ·  Help: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/67?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_series_follow_newsletter_02%3BMpznujDsTsuJqBjxkmWbVg%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=30BHZkN4jUYIg1&trk=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-help-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_series_follow_newsletter_02-help-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mq7ltr5g~h8-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mq7ltr5g-h8\n\n© 2026 LinkedIn Corporation, 1zwnj000 West Maude Avenue, Sunnyvale, CA 94085.\nLinkedIn and the LinkedIn logo are registered trademarks of LinkedIn.','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('af711efb-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear The Zoho Bulletin,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"What will it take for India to build world-class AI?\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('af798494-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Letter from Nthabi - a Forward alumna\nHi Yashica,\n\nNthabi here! :) I got my Forward digital badge and certificate in 2021 and I am a Forward Volunteer Ambassador from Johannesburg, South Africa. \n\nBack then, I almost did not complete the program. I will tell you what I did about it, perhaps it will be helpful for you as the Core Skills level deadline gets closer.\n\nPeople often ask how I avoid burnout from over- committing. \"A jack of all trades but a master of time management\"– that\'s me. I’m in the music industry where I lead a customer experience team. On top of many personal responsibilities, I also volunteer with Forward and against hunger in Africa.\n\nFeeling like you took on too much? I understand and have been there too. I almost did not complete the program on time because of that.\n\nMy solution? Time management. Here\'s the deal:\n\n\n\n	- Sync the upcoming deadline with other commitments (job, school, family). Write them all down to see them in front of you.\n	- Identify a few ‘lighter days’ until then where you can fit in about 2 hours of Forward – weekends, lunch breaks, whatever suits you. Remember, balance in life also means giving yourself permission to rest when tired.\n	- Surround yourself with peers or seek advice from program graduates\n	- Recall why you signed up for Forward in the first place. Write it or say it out loud.\n\n\nMy reason for joining Forward? I joined to evolve as a human (science) alongside an evolving world (artificial intelligence). Forward equips us to strike that harmony.\n\nYour reasons will vary – career growth, emotional management, adapting to change, or curiosity. All are valid, needing commitment and time management.\nYou can follow me on Linkedin <https://links.mckinsey.com/NDczLVpZRS01MjIAAAGiTq6m4xVXU0LhSUfk75REfdVBSdOd1EPkUcK0lzkPKpbqM_paFFIKFWHflHcPLj3QVCLzO6c=> where I post regularly about Forward. You can also reach out to me and I will definitely answer any questions you might have. My LinkedIn page name is Nthabiseng Nyakane <https://links.mckinsey.com/NDczLVpZRS01MjIAAAGiTq6m4xVXU0LhSUfk75REfdVBSdOd1EPkUcK0lzkPKpbqM_paFFIKFWHflHcPLj3QVCLzO6c=>.\n\nSee you at the finish line!\n\n#TakeAStepForward\n#ITookAStepForward\nNeed Help? \n\n You are receiving this email from an account we use for outbound emails only. We have created these resources to help you have a smooth journey:\nFind the answer in our Forward Solution Hub <https://links.mckinsey.com/NDczLVpZRS01MjIAAAGiTq6m4wVPBQiXRDTgV7aJpXfvNfcHKExss1E2JqU957Cvi-qxbcMdgWsjcOqbEj_Dscl1nsE=>\nUse our Forward Solution Hub to find answers to the frequently asked questions.\n\n© McKinsey & Company, Inc. \n 175 Greenwich Street \n New York, NY 10007 \n United States\n\nThis email contains operational information regarding your progress in McKinsey’s Forward Program. By opening our emails or clicking on links you agree to our use of cookies and web tracking technology. For more information on how we use and protect your information, please review our privacy policy <https://www.mckinsey.com/privacy-policy>. If you prefer not to receive future email communications from us, please click here <https://links.mckinsey.com/NDczLVpZRS01MjIAAAGiTq6m46amBBLO5WuDu2blNWIRKeyG56Jv7cPd8YqBrixRyL4HqIqNvhcI2agDjAUL3gBo8kY=> to unsubscribe from all McKinsey communications. Please note, however, that these emails are transactional in nature and are sent while you remain a participant in the program. Unsubscribing from general commercial communications related to McKinsey’s research, insights, services or events will not automatically exclude you from receiving these operational messages, unless you explicitly request otherwise.\n\nThis email was sent to loharyashica@gmail.com. If you no longer wish to receive these emails you may unsubscribe here: https://pages.mckinsey.com/Unsubscribed.html?mkt_unsubscribe=1&mkt_tok=NDczLVpZRS01MjIAAAGiTq6m4xJh7_fe6ypdeiBrf3zMw_38vtWyKl5PUNYr9SVAqhg0FI_3uaOORCKCI_ATdry_S_5548mr3_M6xu2g0atl2EHwM_ZmuTLfi43kECp5eMb90A.\n','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('af7a029b-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear Nthabi - A Forward Alumna,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"Yashica, From Me to You: My Forward Story and Secrets to Success\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('af7dc333-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Student Discount Preference Survey\n\nDear Yashica,\n\nBuddy4Study is planning to launch a Student Discount Zone where you’ll get exclusive offers on products and services you use every day – from online shopping and food delivery to movie tickets, travel, electronics, insurance, and more.\n\nBefore we launch, your opinion matters.\n\nWe want to understand what you actually want discounts on, so we can bring the right brands and the best deals to you.\n\nPlease take 2–3 minutes to fill this quick survey: https://forms.gle/ZhVrVi1DiLUQibYb7 \n\nWhy should you fill it?\n\nHelp us bring relevant discounts for school/college/university students like you\nGet early access to the Student Discount Zone when it goes live\nShape which categories and brands we prioritize first\nYour responses will be kept confidential and used only to improve student-centric offerings on Buddy4Study.\n\nThank you for helping us build a one-stop student discount solution.\n\nWarm regards,\nTeam Buddy4Study','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('af7e5429-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear Buddy4Study,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"Invitation to Fill Student Discount Preference Survey 2026\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('af970bf5-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'  LinkedIn\nSee new openings\n ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌  ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌  ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌  ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌  ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌  ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ \n‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌  ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌  ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ \n\nLinkedIn\n[https://res1.em.linkedin.com/res/tracking/linkedin-blue-200x51.png]https://t1.em.linkedin.com/r/?id=h88074ca7-f863-4af6-91eb-00d7e726b44f,8d2ee6,7d8fa2&e=bWNpZD02ODk2OTU1NzcwMzQ5MzcxMzkyJnRyaz1lbWxfbGlfbUVNX2dsb2JhbF9jYXJlZXJzX2pvYnNndG1fbWt0Z190OWNfYWNxX0phbjIwMjFfdjEmc3JjPWUtZW1s&s=HpvyDoOKBwm4ZH3XI8MYK1uBGqtT49I1R65IrVSqCT4\n[https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D5603AQG6ik6M5nm_Yw/profile-displayphoto-scale_400_400/B56Z0PHzOGKkAk-/0/1774075200293?e=1782345600&v=beta&t=KunBphfeDVfTO86gwCii9MJshk96KzjpMWaxVluZ7ao]https://t1.em.linkedin.com/r/?id=h88074ca7-f863-4af6-91eb-00d7e7