cribe-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_accept_invite_single_01-unsubscribe-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mq9v2a8g~96-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mq9v2a8g-96&loid=AQFFu5EWqkcr8wAAAZ64DRUwA6SE6HuPEDpaEXxuitPRssJZt-r5Qg5bnen6RqI0DVqf-YgcIS-64Oe5wtI4-4rqqXGYR1WGP1y7th8fjn5l\nHelp: https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/67?lang=en&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_accept_invite_single_01%3BvEqHlSIRQ%2F6WrvbtPXyAKw%3D%3D&midToken=AQG-BFco0wt-tA&midSig=1iIzYwOCXi-Yg1&trk=eml-email_accept_invite_single_01-help-0-textfooterglimmer&trkEmail=eml-email_accept_invite_single_01-help-0-textfooterglimmer-null-icq8ji~mq9v2a8g~96-null-null&eid=icq8ji-mq9v2a8g-96&otpToken=MTMwNDFlZTkxNTI5YzljMmJjMjgwZmViNDExNmU2YjY4ZmNhZDM0MzljYTg4NjYyN2JjZjA1Njc0NzU5NTRmYmYwZDBkM2U5NTBjYmM0ZTY3ZjhkZjM5ODAxMzYyYjA2NmE2ZDE1MGRkOTYyNWYxNTJhMWM5ZDJiLDEsMQ%3D%3D\n\n© 2026 LinkedIn Corporation, 1zwnj000 West Maude Avenue, Sunnyvale, CA 94085.\nLinkedIn and the LinkedIn logo are registered trademarks of LinkedIn.','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('afd66c1d-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Dear Kuldeep Tripathi via LinkedIn,\n\nWe have received your ticket regarding: \"Kuldeep  accepted your invitation, explore their network\".\n\nYour reference ID is #d69e6b3d. This issue has been logged and is currently under review by our team.','approved-draft-placeholder','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('afda836d-6633-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7','d69e6b3d-662d-11f1-bb83-601031c340f7',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Restrict unrestricted keys to maintain service continuity.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHello Yashica,\n\nWe are reaching out to remind you because your project currently has the Gemini API ( generativelanguage.googleapis.com ) enabled and contains at least one unrestricted API key. To prevent unauthorized usage, we ask you to restrict all your unrestricted API keys by June 19, 2026. After this deadline, unrestricted keys will no longer be accepted by the Gemini API.\n\nWe\'ve provided additional details below to help you understand these changes and take any necessary actions.\n\nWhat you need to know\n\nWhy is this change necessary\nAPI keys generated by Google AI Studio are restricted by default and can only be used to access the Gemini API. A project that contains additional, unrestricted API keys can pose a risk because these unrestricted keys can also be used to access the Gemini API. Possible impacts may include:\n\n\nFinancial risk: Unauthorized parties using your quota and increasing your bill\nData exposure: Potential access to sensitive AI workloads or conversation histories\n\nPlease refer to the Best practices for managing API Keys guide.\n\nWhat you need to do\n\nAction required by June 19, 2026:\nYou must restrict your unrestricted keys in the AI Studio UI or in the Google Cloud Console by June 19, 2026 to maintain service continuity. After this date, the Gemini API will no longer accept requests that use unrestricted keys. Or, you can alternatively generate new keys in the AI Studio UI and replace old keys in your code.\n\nWe\'re here to help\n\nRefer to the Manage API keys documentation and Secure unrestricted API keys for more information.\n\nBinding keys to a service account is automatically allowed if the API restriction is set to Gemini APIs ( generativelanguage.googleapis.com ) and doesn\'t require changes to Org policy ( constraints/iam.managed.disableServiceAccountApiKeyCreation ). In addition, the Service Account doesn\'t require any Identity and Access Management role grants.\n\nThanks for choosing Google AI Studio and Gemini API.\n\n\n\n\n– The Gemini API Team\n\n\n\n\n\n© 2026 Google LLC 1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043, USA\nThis email was sent to loharyashica@gmail.com because you signed up to try the Gemini API and Google AI Studio.\n\n\n\n\n','incoming-complaint','INCOMING',NULL,'2026-06-21 16:52:16',NULL,NULL,NULL),('af